// The addons' version history as of the day this file was built (tools: build.sh).
// Releases newer than this are read live from GitHub when the page opens.
window.ZAC_CHANGELOG = {"generated":"2026-11-27","addons":{"zacui":{"current":"3.0.20","games":["era","tbc","forever","retail"],"versions":[{"v":"3.0.20","d":"2026-11-25","title":"A website for reports and ideas, and lists that show every choice whole","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"ZacUI has a website: what changed in every version, bug reports and feature suggestions. /zui report and /zui suggest give you the link with your version filled in. So do the buttons under Need help? on the Overview page and the headset button beside Discord and Twitch."},{"t":"Action bars: a key name too long for its button is drawn a little smaller so the whole name shows. A tick under Keys turns it off."},{"t":"Tooltips: a skinnable corpse can show the skinning skill it needs. Off until you turn it on."},{"t":"Bags: items you cannot use can be tinted. Off until you turn it on."},{"t":"Unit frames: the power bar can hide on a target that has no mana, rage or energy. Off until you turn it on."},{"t":"Profiles: an exported profile remembers the screen it was made on, and importing it on a different screen says so."},{"t":"Scrolling text: the extra attacks line (Windfury) is offered on WoW Forever, and /zui combattext lists what the game reports there.","g":["forever"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Dropdown lists are as wide as their longest choice, so nothing in an open list is cut short."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Searching the settings made the game stutter. It no longer does."},{"t":"Dropdown lists opened bigger or smaller than their box when the settings window was not at 100%."},{"t":"Settings window: two page descriptions were cut short, and one row in the unit frames preview's list stuck out."},{"t":"Auction house: the Auctions column heading was cut short.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]}]}]},{"v":"3.0.19","d":"2026-11-22","title":"Timers that catch up when you join late, and easier bag pins","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Pull and break timers: join a group late, or log in while one is running, and the bar catches up. A running break is asked from the group's ZacUI and DBM users, a pull countdown from its ZacUI users."},{"t":"/zui timers shows what the pull and break timers asked for and what came back, for when a bar does not show."},{"t":"Bags: take an item out of the pinned row with the x in its corner while you hold Alt, or right-click the + for a list of everything pinned. The Bags page, Look tab, picks the key."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"A cooldown that began before your PC was restarted showed as a full, greyed cooldown on bag items, bars and trackers. It shows the time really left."},{"t":"Warrior HUD: the second trinket's icon shows its active time, and each trinket icon shows its own trinket's buff. Any trinket you use shows its active time.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Party frames under the Classic, WoW Forever and Blizzard styles: the samples in move mode and in the settings look like the real frames, and the real ones no longer sit off to one side after a size change."},{"t":"Seamless map: an error that could come up while the map window changed size.","g":["era","forever"]}]}],"titles":{"retail":"Timers that catch up when you join late"}},{"v":"3.0.18","d":"2026-11-20","title":"A chat window that stays put in raids","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"With \"Same chat size and spot on every character\" on, the chat window could jump to the game's default place and back over and over in a raid, and the raid or party frames in the chat box went with it or were left out of place until the fight ended. The window stays on its spot."}]}]},{"v":"3.0.17","d":"2026-11-20","title":"A size for every piece on screen, a macro cleaner, and boss loot","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"One size for everything ZacUI puts on screen: a slider on the Movers page and in Edit Mode. It reaches the class HUD, trackers, timers, alerts, consumable bars, unit frames, action bars, nameplates and meter windows."},{"t":"Edit Mode: each piece has its own size. Pick a piece to make it smaller or bigger, or to set its width, height, icon size and spacing right there."},{"t":"Class HUDs: every piece has its own scale, and the mana and energy tick strips have a height.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Macro cleaner: every macro in one list with a tick. Delete many at once, see which ones nothing uses, and bring one back from the bin. Open it with /zui macros or the Clean up button on the macro window."},{"t":"The macro cleaner can also delete by itself: macros another addon keeps making, or macros that have gone unused for a number of days. Off until you turn it on under Quality of life, Macros."},{"t":"Boss loot: a small card of what a boss dropped and who got it. Off until you turn it on under Quality of life."},{"t":"Loot rolls: a card style with the item's name, bind type and time left, and every part of it is a setting. A new install starts with it; yours stays as it was until you pick it."},{"t":"Loot rolls: the need, greed and pass buttons can wear the game's 3D art or flat icons."},{"t":"Seamless map: Map style in its menu, to go back to the game's map or choose again.","g":["era","forever"]},{"t":"Tooltips: a tick to hide the \"Made by\" line on crafted items."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Borders and thin lines are one screen pixel wide at every UI scale."},{"t":"Class HUDs: a new setup places the trinket row where every screen size shows it. A HUD already set up keeps its place.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Bars, timers and other pieces could draw over the open world map. They go behind it now and come back when it closes."},{"t":"Seamless map: dragging the map's header did not move the map.","g":["era","forever"]},{"t":"Changing a meter window's scale from its header menu moved the window. It stays in place."}]}]},{"v":"3.0.16","d":"2026-11-19","title":"Chat that keeps its place and its font, and icon sizes on nameplates","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Nameplates: each debuff group has its own icon size, and icon rows have a setting for the space between icons. Raid mod icons have a size as well."},{"t":"Warrior HUD: the second trinket slot can be added to the buff row.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Hunter HUD: the Auto Shot bar has its own width and height.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Class HUDs: a new setup starts with trinket slot 1 only, and slot 2 is a tick on the page. A HUD already set up keeps what it shows.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"The chat window could jump back to the game's Edit Mode position after a portal, a summon or closing Edit Mode. It stays where you put it, and moving it in Edit Mode is kept."},{"t":"The font picked on Fonts & Textures did not always reach the game's chat windows, or was gone after a reload."},{"t":"A font, size or outline picked for chat messages on the Chat page could be lost after a loading screen."},{"t":"An error at login when another addon's copy of a shared library was broken. The minimap button loads anyway."}]}]},{"v":"3.0.15","d":"2026-11-19","title":"Looks you can pick: window finish, buttons, the minimap's pieces and the button tray","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Style page: the window finish is a choice. Pick a preset (soft depth, flat, dark bands, an accent line under title bars, textured) or set the depth, outlines and one of nine textures yourself."},{"t":"Style page: button depth from flat to deeper, and a plain look for a window's main button."},{"t":"Style page: mouse wheel speed, and smooth scrolling on or off."},{"t":"Minimap: the backing behind the clock, zone name and the other pieces is a choice: solid box, soft shadow, outline only, glass plate, edge fade, or your own."},{"t":"Button tray: it can sit on any edge of the minimap, as a band on the map, or as a tab that opens a grid. It can come out while the mouse is on the map or stay out."},{"t":"Class HUDs: totem timers for Shamans, your own spell, item, buff and debuff icons, marks and the cast's cost on the power bar, a cast bar, and icons that show only with a talent or in a stance or form. All off until you switch them on.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Class HUDs: the game's rotation helper can light the next spell.","g":["forever","retail"]},{"t":"A class resource bar: Holy Power, combo points, Chi, Soul Shards, Essence, Arcane Charges, runes, Stagger and soul fragments. Ironfur and Ignore Pain can show as a time-left bar. Spells with charges show their count.","g":["retail"]},{"t":"Raid timer: \"The clock starts at\" picks between the first fight with a kill and the first time you enter combat.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Readycheck raid configs can hide the damage meter's windows while you are in that raid. The meter keeps counting."},{"t":"Warrior HUD: a cooldown linked to a Readycheck boss reminder reads WAIT until that reminder goes off.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Consumables bar: the Horde mode option is gone. One \"Weapon stones\" switch turns the bar's weapon buttons on or off, and \"Weapons shown\" picks which ones. The main hand button starts hidden only for Horde on Classic Era.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"New installs start with a soft shadow behind the minimap's pieces and the button tray on the minimap's left edge. A setup already in use is unchanged."},{"t":"Raid timer: a boss pull starts the clock even when you are not in combat yet, and it starts when you arrive in the middle of a fight."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Raid timer: a trash skip before the first pull started the clock. A fight with no kill no longer counts as the start.","g":["era","tbc"]}]}]},{"v":"3.0.14","d":"2026-11-16","title":"Windows and buttons with more depth","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"ZacUI's windows have a little shading, lit edges and raised title bars instead of one flat colour. The Style page has a \"Surface finish\" slider; 0% brings the flat windows back."},{"t":"Action bars page, Advanced tab: \"Arrange for this style\" lays your bars out again for the style you picked."},{"t":"Gear slots in the character and inspect windows show each item's level.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"Blizzard style: party frames wear the live game's party frame.","g":["forever","retail"]},{"t":"Blizzard style: the quest tracker wears the live game's art.","g":["forever"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Buttons and the settings window's page rows stand out more: a brighter raised face, a clearer outline and a thin shadow underneath."},{"t":"Popup buttons are raised like every other button. The main choice has a gold face, a destructive one a red face."},{"t":"Bars you have not moved are laid out again when you pick another style. Bars you moved stay where you put them."},{"t":"Under a game style the micro menu and the bag bar are the game's own, where the game puts them. Move them in the game's Edit Mode.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"Under a game style the first action bar stays beside the game's micro menu, with the end cap at the end of the row and the XP bar across it.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"Under Classic WoW UI and Blizzard style the game's windows wear ZacUI's style. Bars, unit frames, chat, minimap and the quest tracker keep the style you picked.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"The character and inspect windows are the game's own, in ZacUI's style.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"The Reputation, Skills, Statistics, Currency and PvP pages are styled.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"New installs start with ZacUI's focus frame on.","g":["tbc","forever","retail"]},{"t":"Under Classic WoW UI and Blizzard style ZacUI's focus frame is switched on once, so it matches the other frames.","g":["forever"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"The merchant window showed an error and overlapped its title.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"The quest window showed the game's frame through ZacUI's.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"The trade window showed the other player's portrait over the header.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"An error when a target's cast was interrupted.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"The stance bar sat left of the gryphon under a game style.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"Minimap zoom jittered.","g":["forever","retail"]},{"t":"Classic WoW UI: a window's bottom tabs were the wrong size.","g":["forever","retail"]},{"t":"Bags under a game style: doubled labels on the Groups and Sort buttons."}]}],"titles":{"forever":"WoW Forever: game styles that fit, and the game's own micro menu and bags"}},{"v":"3.0.12","d":"2026-11-15","title":"Shorter loading screens, a faster threat meter, and game styles on more of the screen","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"The settings window loads when you first open it, so logging in is quicker."},{"t":"The boss mods for the five Classic raids load when you walk into the raid, not at login.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Threat meter: your row, the tank's row and \"You pull at\" update the moment your threat changes."},{"t":"Threat meter: \"Make my row stand out\", with a colour of its own. On the Damage meter page, General tab."},{"t":"Warrior HUD: Blood Fury, Berserking, War Stomp and Will of the Forsaken. On for Horde warriors.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Warrior HUD: Fetish of the Sand Reaver's buff shows on the buff row with the trinket's icon.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Bags: a side-rail window style with a keyring, a pinned row and All, Kind and New views. Bags page, Look tab."},{"t":"World map: a new install is asked which map style to use the first time the map opens.","g":["era","forever"]},{"t":"Under WoW Forever, Blizzard style and Classic WoW UI, ZacUI's raid timers, flight timer, buff reminder tracker, HUD icons and the raid mods' bars and icons now wear that style."},{"t":"/zui perf shows what ZacUI is costing you."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"New installs open ZacUI's windows at 80% size, and popups follow the settings window's size."},{"t":"Every scroll bar is the same grey."},{"t":"The colour picker no longer stutters while you drag."},{"t":"Under a game style the world map is the game's own window. ZacUI's map window and the seamless map are ticks on the Maps page."},{"t":"Under a game style the auction house is the game's own.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"A new install that picks a game style starts on the game's own bags."},{"t":"Raid mods: bars and warnings match ZacUI's look under ZacUI's style.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Warrior HUD: a buff that ends fades out where it stands. No more empty slot on the buff row.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Horde warriors on Classic Era: the Salvation icons and \"Drop Salvation while tanking\" are gone. There are no paladins to give it.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Weapon stones: the menu and tooltip show your pick even when you carry none, and which stone is used instead.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Chat and unit frames do less work while nothing is happening."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"The on/off switches in the settings sidebar did nothing on WoW Forever.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"An error from heal prediction on WoW Forever with OldRaidFrames installed.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"An error from the seamless map when zoomed far in.","g":["era","forever"]},{"t":"A purple ring on weapon stone buffs on the buff bar.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Quick Keybind Mode: Escape no longer leaves the mode, and the game's extra action button no longer takes your key presses."},{"t":"Dropping a spell on a bar in combat no longer raises an \"action blocked\" error. A chat line says to drop it after the fight."},{"t":"The trade window's header matches the other windows."}]}],"titles":{"retail":"Shorter loading screens and game styles on more of the screen"}},{"v":"3.0.11","d":"2026-11-12","title":"A changelog for the game version you play","s":[{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"What's New and the Changelog page list only the changes for the game version you are playing."}]}]},{"v":"3.0.10","d":"2026-11-12","title":"A world-buff switch for the buff remover, and a smoother warrior HUD","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Buff remover: an \"Only while world buffs are out\" switch. With no world buff on you nothing ticked is cancelled; once you have one, everything ticked goes as usual.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Buff remover: while that switch is on, a buff can be marked \"even with no WBs\" so it always goes. Salvation while tanking always goes too.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Hesitation prompts: in execute range, Whirlwind is marked ahead of Execute when there are enough mobs for it. It has its own switch.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Hesitation prompts: a Glide option. The icons over your target fade, slide and grow instead of jumping.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"With Readycheck installed, its route tracker can sit along the top of the chat box in a raid, above the raid frames. The switch is on the Chat page under \"In a raid\", with two more for how gear swaps show on it.","g":["era","tbc"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Warrior HUD: icons grow smoothly, and an icon that leaves keeps its place for a moment so the row does not jump twice.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Every window's resize corner is one solid corner that lights up under the mouse and while you drag it."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"A first login no longer ticks buffs for removal on a warrior, changes attack macros or makes a macro called \"dummy\".","g":["era"]},{"t":"Hesitation prompts: an ability that comes off cooldown during the global cooldown counts as ready.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Hesitation prompts: Arms warriors get Mortal Strike where Bloodthirst would be.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Hesitation prompts: Whirlwind was rated too high with a fast main-hand weapon.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"The map window's title bar no longer shows a lighter slab behind it."},{"t":"Auction house: the line saying what you bought no longer flickers while buying stacks.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"Whirlwind over Execute, and a smoother warrior HUD","forever":"Whirlwind over Execute, and a smoother warrior HUD","retail":"A solid resize corner"}},{"v":"3.0.9","d":"2026-11-11","title":"The old raid frames, and one look everywhere","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"With the Classic WoW UI style your raid uses the old Blizzard raid frames: class colours, groups four across, pets and main tanks. /orf opens their options."},{"t":"Edit Mode: a Previews button shows or hides what is drawn under the boxes, and each frame's preview can be switched on its own. Right-click a frame in the Frames list."},{"t":"Edit Mode: the party preview and the raid preview each have their own switch."},{"t":"The bags and the auction house show an icon on their title bar."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The game's Options window matches ZacUI's settings window."},{"t":"Checkboxes, dropdowns, sliders, tabs and text boxes look the same everywhere, inside the settings window and out."},{"t":"Game windows that ZacUI restyles have their title at the left in ZacUI's font, over the same flat header as ZacUI's own windows."},{"t":"The bar under the chat and the button column beside it are solid. The chat itself stays see-through."},{"t":"The damage meter's menu page is the same grey as the other windows."},{"t":"Dark window colours saved by older versions give way to the new lighter ones. Colours you picked yourself are kept."},{"t":"The first-time tips in the settings window open beside it instead of over the tabs."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Buff remover: going to Defensive Stance and straight back no longer cancels Salvation.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Edit Mode: a small slip of the mouse while clicking a frame no longer moves it."},{"t":"The auction buying window keeps its size when you press Buy.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"The damage meter preview's size note no longer sits under the Layout button."},{"t":"The mail windows have ZacUI's scroll bars."}]}]},{"v":"3.0.8","d":"2026-11-10","title":"Class HUDs for your spec, and a buff filter","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Every class HUD starts on your spec's own list, with separate lists for Classic Era, TBC and WoW Forever.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Warrior, priest and paladin HUDs follow your spec too. Characters that already use them keep exactly what they had.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Warrior HUD: a row for debuffs on your target, such as Sunder Armor stacks and Demoralizing Shout.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"Priest HUD: a row for your own buffs. Paladin HUD: a row for your judgements on the target.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"A \"Show spells you haven't learned yet\" option on every class HUD."},{"t":"A first class HUD for Retail, for all classes. It is off until you switch it on and has not been tested in the game yet.","g":["retail"]},{"t":"A filter for buffs and debuffs on unit frames and on the nameplates' simple debuff row: pick what shows, add spells to always or never show, and set limits. Your old settings carry over."},{"t":"Edit Mode has a bar across the top, and the box you click shows its own actions. Class HUDs show their real icons while you place them."},{"t":"The raid mods' boxes stay out of Edit Mode until you press \"Raid mods\" on the bar.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Bags can be split into groups by kind with the Groups button. New items get a gold edge, and a small bar shows how full your bags are."},{"t":"The auction buy window shows the item's quality and a progress bar, and can list every auction it will buy.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"TBC raid mods are filled out for all nine raids, Karazhan to Sunwell: cast bars with a KICK mark, debuff lists, tank icons, stand-in-it alarms and many more boss timers.","g":["tbc"]},{"t":"Buff reminders on TBC: Commanding Shout, Earth Shield and the Master Soulstone. Fear Ward for priests who know it.","g":["tbc"]},{"t":"Buff reminders can be limited to TBC's raids.","g":["tbc"]},{"t":"Your own buffs and debuffs by the minimap can use the buff filter, and party and raid frames can have a filter of their own."},{"t":"A \"Seen lately\" list on the filter page: always show or never show a buff with one click."},{"t":"Bags: an option to put Search and Sort on the title bar."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The settings window has a new look: sidebar pages, tabs and buttons are proper buttons, and section titles have a line across the page."},{"t":"Custom nameplate debuffs can be added by name as well as by spell ID."},{"t":"The window's corner buttons (reload, size, fold, close) are small raised buttons."},{"t":"Options that do nothing on a game version are hidden on that version."},{"t":"The Darkmoon Faire mark on the damage meter hides while you have the fortune yourself, and is offered on Classic Era only.","g":["era"]},{"t":"The \"What's New\" window and the scroll bars match Readycheck's."},{"t":"The map and the skinned game windows have the same flat header as the rest of ZacUI."},{"t":"Edit Mode is easier to use: a line under the bar says how it works, the list shows what you can move first, and the box you click only offers what it can do."},{"t":"Windows outside the settings window are a lighter grey instead of near-black."},{"t":"The auction buying window is much smaller.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"On a fresh install more frames start in spots where they don't overlap. Setups you already have are not moved."},{"t":"The settings search remembers what it has read, so it no longer stalls the first time you search each session."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Several class HUD icons that tracked the wrong spell or never lit up, mostly on TBC."},{"t":"Updating no longer changes the nameplate sizes you already had."},{"t":"Scrolling a long page no longer slows down near the top and bottom."},{"t":"Slider handles were dark instead of gold."},{"t":"A line no longer runs through the percent text on the nameplate threat bar."},{"t":"Retail: the backpack icon was invisible, bag icons had black corners, and a gold line crossed the character window.","g":["retail"]},{"t":"Typing in the bag search or the Edit Mode search no longer lags."},{"t":"Text on the Edit Mode bar no longer overlaps."},{"t":"Features that are switched on can be placed in Edit Mode before they first appear."}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"TBC raid mods, and class HUDs for your spec","retail":"A first class HUD for Retail, and a buff filter"}},{"v":"3.0.6","d":"2026-11-09","title":"Move the previews around","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Drag a settings preview to move it around while you're zoomed in."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Releases reach CurseForge again: 3.0.3 to 3.0.5 never made it there, and everything in them is in this version."}]}]},{"v":"3.0.5","d":"2026-11-08","title":"Clear nameplate bars","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Nameplates under the game styles show nothing behind the missing health - no grey backing or white wash."},{"t":"Nameplates under the Forever and live styles use the game's own bar art."},{"t":"The game options window under the 2004 style has one close button, not two."},{"t":"Quest and gossip text under the game styles is no longer heavy black."},{"t":"No more blocked-action error when hovering an action button in combat."},{"t":"Action bar icons under the live style on WoW Forever fill their slots again.","g":["forever"]}]}]},{"v":"3.0.4","d":"2026-11-08","title":"Party frames and a new buy window","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Scroll the mouse wheel over a settings preview to zoom it in and out."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Party frames wear the game's own small party frame under the Classic, WoW Forever and Blizzard styles."},{"t":"The auction house buy window is redesigned: the item with its icon, what you've bought and spent, and one clear price button.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"The key ring is a square slot with its own icon, like the bags beside it."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Nameplates under the game styles have nothing behind the health bar, and no white wash on your target."},{"t":"Party power bars (rage, energy, mana) show under the game styles instead of a white bar."}]}]},{"v":"3.0.3","d":"2026-11-08","title":"Sharper buttons and a Twitch link","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"A Twitch button next to the Discord one in the settings."},{"t":"Classic WoW UI: the original stone bar behind the main action bar."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Close buttons, switches and slider knobs are sharper at any UI scale."},{"t":"Settings: Reload and the window's size are small icons in the header; the bar along the bottom is gone."},{"t":"The colour picker is smooth, and right-clicking a colour box resets it."},{"t":"Small popups have a smaller close button, and their buttons always show."},{"t":"Chat: the icons sit in a column joined to the chat's left side and show when the mouse is over the chat (the Chat page can keep them always up). The Party / Chat / Hide msgs buttons over the chat are gone - the icons do the same jobs."},{"t":"Style page: a part ticked under a look can be unticked again."},{"t":"The \"Move in Edit Mode\" tag on the settings pages is gone; Edit Mode is in the sidebar."},{"t":"Windows use the flat header from the settings, with no sparkle."},{"t":"Bags under the WoW Forever and Blizzard looks use the game's own bag window: the portrait, rim, title, close button and coin box."},{"t":"Classic WoW UI on WoW Forever: the minimap gets the 2004 grey ring and zone bar, the character pane and spellbook the 2004 look, and the bag bar and menu buttons their 2004 art.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"Nameplates: the hesitation icons sit above the mob's name instead of on it, and Demoralizing Shout shows with your other debuffs under the bar."},{"t":"The changelog window is more compact."},{"t":"Classic WoW UI on WoW Forever: the game's own windows (character, spellbook, vendors, quests, mail, bank, friends, options, popups, tooltips and more) wear the 2004 border, gold title, round close button, old tabs and old buttons.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"Known issue: a few windows may still not fully match the look you picked (the world map keeps ZacUI's own frame). Keep sending screenshots."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Buffs and the bag bar were not getting ZacUI's look on Era and TBC.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"A second close button on the loot window on Era and TBC.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Square corners on the nameplate target glow."},{"t":"The colour picker's colour wheel was blank on Era and TBC, and the picker could open behind the settings.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The mount button on Era and TBC used a call that only works on WoW Forever and never mounted you; it uses your mount from your bags again.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The auction house buy window: the Buy button no longer covers the text, and it shows the amount and price again.","g":["era","tbc","forever"]},{"t":"An error in the unit frame preview."}]}]},{"v":"3.0.2","d":"2026-11-08","title":"Quieter starting settings","s":[{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"A fresh install starts with the warrior HUD, the hesitation prompts, the threat screen glow and scrolling combat text off. Each one can be turned on in the settings."}]}]},{"v":"3.0.1","d":"2026-11-08","title":"A smoother setup and better starting settings","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"A Discord button to contact Zac for help."},{"t":"Chat: buttons on the rail to swap between the chat and the raid frames."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The first-time setup is one flow: pick a look, pick your parts, done."},{"t":"Popups and their headers match the new settings window."},{"t":"Bags and the bank follow the look you pick."},{"t":"The chat rail sits on the right of the chat and never changes the chat's size."},{"t":"A fresh install starts with one damage meter window, the threat window closed and the minimap button tray off."},{"t":"A fresh install under the ZacUI look gets a clean action bar layout, shorter unit frames and cleaner nameplates, and the game's own damage meter stays hidden."},{"t":"The XP bar is never wider than the main action bar."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"An error from nameplates on WoW Forever.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"An error from the chat rail at login."},{"t":"Tooltip boxes in the settings showing white."},{"t":"Overlapping pieces in the settings preview."}]}]},{"v":"3.0.0","d":"2026-11-08","title":"Looks, a new settings window and a polish pass on everything","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Pick a look: ZacUI, Classic WoW UI, WoW Forever (on Forever) or Blizzard style. Each one draws the unit frames, nameplates, action bars, buffs and windows in that style, and starts out looking like the real thing."},{"t":"Classic WoW UI: the original player, target and target-of-target frames with round portraits, the original action buttons and the gryphons at the ends of the main bar."},{"t":"WoW Forever and Blizzard style: the client's own frame, button, bar and nameplate art."},{"t":"The look cards on the Style page and in the setup wizard preview the style before you reload."},{"t":"Chat: an icon rail beside the chat with friends (and how many are online), copy chat, chat settings and scroll to newest. Guild, durability, channels and the chat menu can be added. Everything can be turned off."},{"t":"Chat: a polished style for the panel, tabs and text, on by default and one switch to turn off."},{"t":"Damage meter: on WoW Forever and Retail, the game's own meter is used by default under the Forever and Blizzard looks. The Meter page lets you pick either one.","g":["forever","retail"]},{"t":"Damage meter: a Classic-style meter for the Classic look."},{"t":"Quests: hand-in and accept for you (never picks a reward or pays gold), objective and quest-complete sounds, progress told to your party, and the quest tracker hidden in raids."},{"t":"Alerts: entering and leaving combat, group members dying, the instance reset line, and the screenshot text hidden."},{"t":"Reminders for no pet, a pet on passive, nothing tracked, and low mana on a ready check."},{"t":"A junk window listing your cheapest items to delete when your bags are full."},{"t":"Character stats on screen, cursor rings, a target distance readout, and clock, coordinates, XP and supplies blocks for the chat bar."},{"t":"Repair from guild funds, the skill a herb or ore node needs on its tooltip, and item level and BoE on gear in your bags."},{"t":"Game art settings for the action bars: the gryphons and the bar frame can be turned on or off per bar."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"A new settings window: bigger, with a sidebar, search, a pinned page title, banded rows and new round switches and sliders."},{"t":"Turning a part on or off from the sidebar uses a small switch."},{"t":"Unit frames, nameplates, action bars, buffs, consumables and buff reminders were reworked to a cleaner, sharper look under the ZacUI look."},{"t":"Dragging things in the settings preview is much more accurate: pieces follow the cursor exactly, snapping only grabs nearby pieces, icons swap at the right moment and Escape cancels a drag."},{"t":"Damage meter: the header no longer cuts off the name, mode tiles read in full on narrow windows, and the breakdown is now an easy-to-read table."},{"t":"Icons are cropped a little more so the game's icon border never shows."},{"t":"Bag bar and micro menu start where the game's own sat on a fresh install."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Text on unit frames keeps its black outline."},{"t":"Frames you had placed or sized are never moved or resized by an update."},{"t":"A Classic setup no longer picks up ZacUI-look styling."},{"t":"Several checkboxes that could not be turned off now can."},{"t":"Reset ZacUI now opens the setup wizard afterwards."},{"t":"A minimap button error some players saw at login."}]}]},{"v":"2.0.0","d":"2026-11-01","title":"Changelog","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"A changelog. What is new in each version shows here, and once after you update."}]}]}]},"readycheck":{"current":"5.0.14","games":["era","tbc","forever"],"versions":[{"v":"5.0.14","d":"2026-11-25","title":"A tidier settings window, and a website for reports and ideas","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Readycheck has a website: what changed in every version, bug reports and feature suggestions. /rc report and /rc suggest give you the link with your version filled in. So do the buttons under Need help? on the General page and the headset button beside Discord and Twitch."},{"t":"Gold: pick whose gold counts, on the stats bar's Gold tab. Every account in your mesh is listed. An account on another Battle.net counts once each of the two accounts ticks the other, and a tick carries to your other accounts on the same Battle.net. An account on your Battle.net that is not yours can be unticked."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The group pages (Reminders, Consumables, Gear and the rest) have a new look: each feature is a raised tile with its state, its switch and an In menu tick that takes its page out of the menu on the left."},{"t":"Dropdown lists are as wide as their longest choice, so nothing in an open list is cut short."},{"t":"Appearance: the window preview shows the settings window as it looks today."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Searching the settings made the game stutter. It no longer does."},{"t":"Settings window: text that did not show or was cut short on many pages, among them the description lines on the Sound tab, the Icon look picker, the raid profile box and smart macro lines."},{"t":"Raid pages and the Custom Reminders page were missing their title."},{"t":"Dropdown lists opened bigger or smaller than their box when the settings window was not at 100%."},{"t":"Thin lines in the settings window came and went as it scrolled on some screens."},{"t":"Raid Buff Tracker and Boss Debuff Tracker: the time and the word MISSING were cut short. When a name and MISSING do not both fit, missing rows show an X."},{"t":"Battle Shout tracker: long names were cut short.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Reminder icons and Raid Consume Reminders: a label wider than its icon was cut short."},{"t":"World Buff Drops: your own character's row showed only \"(you)\", and a long name from another realm ran into the level column.","g":["era"]},{"t":"World buff board: the Stored and Ready captions were cut short.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Flask of the Titans, Spirit of Zanza and the Missing Buff Alert preset showed a blank icon."}]}]},{"v":"5.0.13","d":"2026-11-22","title":"Cooldowns after a PC restart","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"A cooldown that began before your PC was restarted could show as a full cooldown on trinket, consumable and item timers. It shows the time really left."}]}]},{"v":"5.0.12","d":"2026-11-20","title":"Gear by spec and stance, and a size for every piece on screen","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Gear Manager, Spec & Stance: say which specs and stances or forms each gear set and item is for, and the dockable buttons' menus list only what fits what you are doing. For every class. Off until you turn it on."},{"t":"Gear sets can go on by themselves when your stance, form or spec changes. In a fight the swap waits for the fight to end, and a rule's Macro button makes one key that changes stance and weapons together. Off until you turn it on."},{"t":"One size for everything Readycheck puts on screen: the Size slider in move mode."},{"t":"Move mode: each piece has its own size. Pick a piece to change its scale, or its width, height, icon size and spacing."},{"t":"Appearance: borders can be a hairline or grow with the UI scale."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Borders and thin lines are one screen pixel wide at every UI scale."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Reminders, dock buttons and other pieces could draw over the open world map. They go behind it now and come back when it closes."},{"t":"Songflower timers could be up to ten seconds late.","g":["era"]},{"t":"The reminder popup's icon size and spacing apply at once, and move mode shows the popup at its real size."},{"t":"Changing a piece's Scale on its page moved the piece. It stays in place."}]}]},{"v":"5.0.11","d":"2026-11-19","title":"Icon sizes for nameplate debuffs","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Nameplates: each debuff group has its own icon size, and icon rows have a setting for the space between icons. Until you set one, the icon follows the text size as before.","g":["era","tbc"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"An error at login when another addon's copy of a shared library was broken. The minimap button loads anyway."}]}],"titles":{"forever":"A login error fixed"}},{"v":"5.0.10","d":"2026-11-19","title":"Smart keys for bosses, World Buff Drops, and a window look you can pick","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Smart keys: link a bar button to an ability on a boss's page. On a boss where that ability is switched off the button does nothing; everywhere else it works as you made it. Click a button on a preview of your bars to link it, or tick Automatic to have it found.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"A linked button reads WAIT on your bars until that ability's reminder goes off on the boss.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"A boss's new Macros page, and a route step, can switch a smart macro, a group of them or a bar slot to one item, such as the potion for that boss. Smart macros can be put in groups.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"World Buff Drops page: which of your characters can still hand in a head or heart, and which already have. It lists level 60s to start with; pick a lower level to see more.","g":["era"]},{"t":"A raid config can hide your damage meter's windows while you are in that raid: Manage, \"Damage meter...\". The meter keeps counting, and the windows come back when you leave or pick another config.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Appearance: a \"Window look\" card. Pick a finish preset or set the depth, outlines and texture yourself, and choose button depth, the main button's look, wheel speed and smooth scrolling."},{"t":"After the raid: buffs that are not on you keep their place, dimmed, so the icons do not move when you click one off. Settings pick which are shown and how dim.","g":["era"]},{"t":"After the raid: the window shows the Chronoboon's cooldown. A setting keeps the Boon button live during it.","g":["era"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Readycheck's windows have raised title bars, and every dialog's main button has the gold face."},{"t":"The What's New window is smaller and scrolls."},{"t":"Consumables bar: the Horde mode option is gone. \"Weapon stones on this bar\" turns its weapon buttons on or off. The main hand button starts hidden only for Horde on Classic Era."},{"t":"Raid consume reminders start switched off on a new profile."},{"t":"Smart Macros has its own icon."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"The mouse wheel moved the settings window only part of a notch. Popups and lists scroll smoothly as well."},{"t":"On a raid's pages the content scrolled under the window's corner buttons.","g":["era","tbc"]}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"Smart keys for bosses, and a window look you can pick","forever":"A window look you can pick"}},{"v":"5.0.9","d":"2026-11-16","title":"Windows and buttons with more depth","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"A chat line when your Darkmoon Faire lockout is pushed off. It has its own row, \"Lockout pushed off\", with the other alerts.","g":["era"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Readycheck's windows have a little shading and a lit top edge instead of one flat colour."},{"t":"Buttons and the sidebar's page rows stand out more: a brighter raised face, a clearer outline and a thin shadow underneath."},{"t":"Popup buttons are raised like every other button. The main choice has a gold face, a destructive one a red face."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"The Darkmoon Faire lockout leaves the world buff board as soon as a full debuff bar pushes it off, and no longer comes back.","g":["era"]}]}]},{"v":"5.0.8","d":"2026-11-15","title":"World buffs after the raid, and a new Edit Mode","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"After the raid: a window with the world buffs still on you. Boon them all with one click, or click a buff to remove it. It opens when you leave the raid or kill the last boss. Off by default: Chronoboon, Behavior, \"After the raid\".","g":["era"]},{"t":"Raid Consume Reminders: \"Only while my world buffs are out\".","g":["era"]},{"t":"Edit Mode has a bar along the top: find a frame by name, Grid, Snap, the Frames list, Undo, Cancel and Save & Exit."},{"t":"Edit Mode: the arrow keys nudge the picked frame (hold Shift for bigger steps) and Ctrl+Z undoes."},{"t":"Changelog: a \"Show all versions\" box in place of the View Full Changelog button."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"A new character opens Readycheck's windows at 80% size, and popups follow the main window's size."},{"t":"Every scroll bar is the same grey."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Importing settings now keeps the gear manager's settings."},{"t":"Fixed an error when the font list holds a font this game client does not have."},{"t":"The Darkmoon Faire timer now resets after 8 hours logged out in a rested place, as the game's does.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Sayge: with a buff picked, the written fortune is no longer taken as well.","g":["era"]}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"A new Edit Mode","forever":"A new Edit Mode"}},{"v":"5.0.7","d":"2026-11-12","title":"A changelog for the game version you play","s":[{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"What's New and the Changelog page list only the changes for the game version you are playing."}]}]},{"v":"5.0.6","d":"2026-11-12","title":"Standing route reminders, and timers that work with Nova again","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Raid routes: standing reminders. A line such as \"hold your potion\" stays on the tracker from one step until a later one. Add it from a step's Add action menu.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Route tracker, bar style: when your gear is swapped, a tick and the set's name show beside the step.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Route tracker, bar style: for a few seconds after a swap the bar shows everything you are wearing, with the pieces that changed lit. Both have a switch on the route's Settings tab.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Buff Timer Network: the Status card says which timer format is in use and warns when other players are on a newer one.","g":["era"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Buff Timer Network: timers are shared in the format the current Nova World Buffs uses, so they pass between the two addons again. Older Readycheck versions need this update to keep receiving.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Every window's resize corner is one solid corner that lights up under the mouse and while you drag it."},{"t":"Route tracker, bar style: the bar is one row shorter. The old gear swap line under it is gone.","g":["era","tbc"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Songflower and other world buff timers were missing with a current Nova World Buffs installed.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Route settings: the Auto width button no longer sits on the scale slider.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Route tracker: \"show the next step\" works as soon as it is ticked.","g":["era","tbc"]}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"Standing route reminders","forever":"A solid resize corner"}},{"v":"5.0.5","d":"2026-11-11","title":"One look for every control, and after-kill gear sets","s":[{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Checkboxes, dropdowns, sliders, tabs and text boxes look the same everywhere, inside the settings window and out."},{"t":"Buttons and close buttons outside the settings window match the ones inside it."},{"t":"Dark colours saved by older versions give way to the new lighter ones. Colours you picked yourself are kept."},{"t":"The stats bar's background is the same grey as the windows."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"A gear set meant for after one boss no longer goes on after a later boss that has none set.","g":["era","tbc"]}]}],"titles":{"forever":"One look for every control"}},{"v":"5.0.4","d":"2026-11-10","title":"Commanding Shout, lighter windows and a faster search","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"TBC: the Battle Shout reminder can watch Commanding Shout instead. Pick the shout you keep up on its page.","g":["tbc"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The pages in the sidebar are proper buttons, with a gold edge under the mouse and on the open page."},{"t":"Tabs are raised buttons with a gold line on the open one."},{"t":"Section titles have a gold mark and a line across the page."},{"t":"Buttons have a raised face."},{"t":"The window's corner buttons (reload, size, fold, close) are small raised buttons."},{"t":"The Gear Manager's tabs match the rest of the window."},{"t":"The \"What's New\" window's buttons match ZacUI's."},{"t":"Options that do nothing on a game version are hidden on that version."},{"t":"Spec detection lists your talents on TBC and reads the new talent tree on WoW Forever.","g":["tbc","forever"]},{"t":"The consumables checker, the bars and the trackers are a lighter grey instead of near-black."},{"t":"On a new character more frames start in spots where they don't overlap. Characters you already have are not moved."},{"t":"The settings search remembers what it has read, so it no longer stalls the first time you search each session."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"The preview's small buttons no longer sit under the window's reload and close icons."},{"t":"The settings window was darker than ZacUI's. It now uses the same colour."},{"t":"Scrolling a long page no longer slows down near the top and bottom."},{"t":"Slider handles have a thin dark outline."},{"t":"The window's size is kept when you reopen it."},{"t":"Typing in the settings search no longer lags."},{"t":"The close button no longer glows white under the mouse, and the reload button is the same height as the others."},{"t":"Sapphiron's reminders were greyed out on game versions without Polarity Mode."}]}]},{"v":"5.0.2","d":"2026-11-08","title":"A cleaner settings window","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"A Twitch button next to the Discord one."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Reload and the window's size are in the header; the extra Close button at the bottom is gone."},{"t":"A sharper close button that matches ZacUI's."},{"t":"Scrolling the settings is faster, and speeds up when you spin the wheel quickly."},{"t":"The Discord and Twitch buttons sit next to the version number."},{"t":"Known issue: some popups still don't fully match the new settings style. A full styling pass is coming in the next update."}]}]},{"v":"5.0.1","d":"2026-11-08","title":"A smoother setup","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"A Discord button to contact Zac for help."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The first-time setup is one short, smooth flow."},{"t":"Popups and their headers match the new settings window."}]}]},{"v":"5.0.0","d":"2026-11-08","title":"A new settings window","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"A new settings window: bigger, with a sidebar, the page title pinned at the top, banded rows, round sliders and a thin scrollbar. Drag it from anywhere, fold it down to its name, and change its scale from the bottom bar."},{"t":"Search every setting from the box at the top of the sidebar, with each result showing where it lives."},{"t":"Raid consume reminders: in a raid, the important consumables you are not using show in the reminders bar."},{"t":"More features now work on TBC Anniversary and WoW Forever instead of switching off.","g":["tbc","forever"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"On WoW Forever, the Battle Shout tracker counts the whole raid, since the shout reaches everyone nearby there.","g":["forever"]},{"t":"A reworked first-time setup."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"An error from the minimap button some players saw at login."}]}]},{"v":"4.9.0","d":"2026-11-06","title":"TBC Anniversary and WoW Forever, and customize everything","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Readycheck now runs on TBC Anniversary and WoW Forever as well as Classic Era."},{"t":"Features that only make sense in Classic Era switch themselves off on TBC and Forever, and their pages say why. This covers world buffs, Chronoboon, Classic raid boss setups and raid routes."},{"t":"Type /rc flavor to see which features are on for your game version."},{"t":"Consumables follow your game version. TBC and Forever get their own items, potions, stones, oils and poisons on the bars, in the checker and in the reminders.","g":["tbc","forever"]},{"t":"In TBC, a battle elixir and a guardian elixir no longer count as clashing. A flask covers both.","g":["tbc"]},{"t":"Almost every text can now be moved and reworded: bar button texts and timers, the reminder popup, the raid buff and boss debuff trackers, the TTK display, the stats bar, the route tracker, the repair reminder, nameplate auras, the consumables checker, gear buttons and the World Buffs board."},{"t":"Most bars and windows have fade, opacity, shadow, glow, layer and scale settings."},{"t":"The reminder popup can grow in any direction and has its own look for each state."},{"t":"The raid buff and boss debuff trackers can change their look as time runs low and play an urgent sound."},{"t":"Live previews for every visual feature, including the World Buffs board, the consumables checker window, world map pins, the minimap button, the stats bar buff list and the gear set picker."},{"t":"Move mode now includes the spec popup, the must-have items alert and the gear swap notice, and shows the position while you drag."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Settings pages are split into tabs, and rows of buttons that picked a value are now dropdowns."},{"t":"Checkboxes and tabs have a cleaner look with a gold tick."},{"t":"Previews take up less room."},{"t":"Settings pages use less memory."},{"t":"In TBC, poisons no longer warn about low charges, since they last an hour.","g":["tbc"]},{"t":"A finished raid route shows the last gear swap, then folds the tracker bar away.","g":["era","tbc"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Weapon stone and oil buttons could click a game popup while you were dead."},{"t":"Consumables bar buttons didn't resize when you changed the button size."},{"t":"Some previews were blank."},{"t":"Previews could flicker while a page resized."},{"t":"\"Can't measure restricted regions\" errors from nameplate auras and animations."},{"t":"Boss buttons on the raid page could overlap.","g":["era","tbc"]}]}]},{"v":"4.8.4","d":"2026-10-25","title":"Smoother gear swaps and raid config fixes","s":[{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Less lag in raids. Looting, zoning and procs are much lighter on your game."},{"t":"Consumable voice warnings now play at your Show before expiry time. Short buffs are called out as soon as you use them."},{"t":"Raid configs now show a boss as set up when it only has gear swaps.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Item lists in raid configs and routes only show what's in your bags, plus one Target Dummy.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The next-trinket icon on the gear buttons is smaller, and the button text shows on top of it."},{"t":"Trinket swaps show right away on both the trinket bar and the gear buttons."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Gear swaps queued in combat could put on the wrong item if your bags changed."},{"t":"Picking a trinket in combat on both the gear buttons and the trinket bar put both on after combat. Now only your last pick counts."},{"t":"Clicking the item in your other trinket, ring or weapon slot in a gear button's menu did nothing. Now it swaps them."},{"t":"A gear button's menu opened right after a swap could show your old items."},{"t":"Taking gear off could fail if your first free bag slot was in a herb, ammo or soul bag."},{"t":"Trinket auto-swap could hold a used trinket for 30 seconds after its buff was gone."},{"t":"Voice warnings for short buffs played too late."},{"t":"Countdown numbers could get stuck on consumables bar buttons."},{"t":"Weapons in your bags could be missing from the weapons bar after logging in."},{"t":"After-kill and on-target consumable reminders didn't work if you carried a different version of the item.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Raid config: the shared Four Horsemen setup could stop working, route gear sets sometimes weren't put on, and the raid page could edit the wrong profile or go blank.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Changing the font could make some text the wrong size."}]}]},{"v":"4.8.3","d":"2026-10-23","title":"Thaddius timer, new route tracker, rogue poisons","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Polarity Mode: a timer starts when Thaddius dies and counts down to your Death Wish, then to Sapphiron. Turn it on or off on the Polarity Mode Sources tab.","g":["era"]},{"t":"A new route tracker: a small panel or a one-row bar, with each mob's kill count and what happens when the step is done.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Kill times remember the class you played. Predictions can use only your class's kills, or include kills from related raid setups.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Rogue poisons on the weapons and consumables bars, with a separate poison for each hand and a warning when the time or the charges run low."},{"t":"Class items for every class in the consumables checker."},{"t":"More looks for the reminder icons: border style, glow size and colours, under Reminders > Position > Icon Display."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Consumable voice warnings were rebuilt so they are no longer skipped, and voice alerts that come at the same moment wait their turn instead of being lost."},{"t":"Trinket auto-swap no longer takes off a trinket that is ready to use or still active. Set your own priority number for each trinket, or pick by list order instead."},{"t":"A consumable used with a keybind, a macro or from your bags shows its cooldown on the consumables bar."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Polarity Mode picks up DBM and BigWigs pull timers again.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Syncing raid profiles with a raid mate no longer turns your routes off.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"An error in combat when a consumable buff ran out, which also stopped the consumables bar updating after the fight."},{"t":"Some weapon oils and poisons showed the wrong name."},{"t":"Bars with their background turned off can be moved right up to the edge of the screen."},{"t":"Searching the settings for a raid boss works again.","g":["era","tbc"]}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"A new route tracker, and rogue poisons","forever":"Rogue poisons"}},{"v":"4.8.2","d":"2026-10-15","title":"Hide gear from menus, buff push-off history, quieter alerts","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Hide items and gear sets from the gear button hover menus: Ctrl+Right-click them. Hold Shift over the menu to see them again."},{"t":"Buff cap: the last 40 buffs that got pushed off, what pushed them and where, on the stats bar settings page.","g":["era"]},{"t":"The consumables and potion bars can now fit up to 40 buttons in a row."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The repair reminder stays out of the way in combat and shows after the fight."},{"t":"Short potions now warn just before they run out, not a minute early."},{"t":"World buff \"cooldown ready\" and \"dropped elsewhere\" alerts are silent again. You can still pick a sound for them.","g":["era"]},{"t":"The minimap icon flips over when you mouse over it, like the icon on the windows."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Voice alerts no longer say \"Potion\" while your potions are on cooldown."},{"t":"Items you hid from the bars no longer get voice alerts."},{"t":"Trinket reminders no longer repeat over and over for trinkets you can't use."},{"t":"Routes: a kill step no longer gets skipped when the same mob is in two steps in a row.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The main hand and off hand stone buttons show the right weapon after a swap."}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"Hide gear from menus, quieter alerts","forever":"Hide gear from menus, quieter alerts"}},{"v":"4.8.1","d":"2026-10-11","title":"Routes from Warcraft Logs, must-have items, buff cap counter","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Build a raid route from a Warcraft Logs report on the website: Routes > From Logs.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Copy my character: one string that takes your gear and consumables to the website."},{"t":"Buff cap counter on the stats bar, with a warning when a buff gets pushed off.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Must-have items: big icons in the middle of your screen if you enter a raid without one."},{"t":"Default list: LIP, Elixir of Poison Resistance, target dummy. Edit it in Consumables Checker."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The weapon skill warning only shows when you zone into a raid."},{"t":"The in-game raid map and route builder are gone; the website does both better.","g":["era","tbc"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Throwing Dynamite no longer makes the consumables bar announce Holy Water."},{"t":"No more LibSharedMedia errors at login next to WeakAuras."}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"Routes from Warcraft Logs, and must-have items","forever":"Must-have items"}},{"v":"4.8.0","d":"2026-10-05","title":"Buff and debuff trackers, hotswap queue, smoother swaps","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Raid Buff Tracker: shows how long your raid buffs have left and warns you before they run out."},{"t":"Boss Debuff Tracker: shows the raid's debuffs on the boss and warns you when one is about to drop.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Both trackers can whisper whoever cast a buff or debuff when it runs out. Off by default."},{"t":"Hotswap macros now work in combat: the gear swap waits and happens when combat ends."},{"t":"Gear waiting to be swapped is shown on your gear buttons and character sheet."},{"t":"Settings search now finds single options and jumps to them."},{"t":"New installs get a short tour of the settings window. Replay it with /rc tutorial."},{"t":"A boss can ask which gear set to wear next when it dies.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Warning when your Darkmoon Faire debuff gets pushed off.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Move or copy kill history between raid profiles.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Reminder icons have a glow you can set to pulse, stay steady or turn off."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Gear and trinket swaps show instantly and fade in smoothly."},{"t":"Nameplate debuff icons run much faster in big pulls."},{"t":"Consumables Checker pop-ups got the new look."},{"t":"Cleaner gear swap menu."},{"t":"New look for window title bars and the character stats bar."},{"t":"Gear set icons show everywhere a set is listed."},{"t":"Kill history is a compact paged list and stays fast with lots of kills.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The minimap button's menu lists every settings page."},{"t":"Save & lock in Edit Mode now locks every bar."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"No more false 'gear swap failed' message after a boss."},{"t":"Battle Shout tracker shows the right attack power.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"World buff board: Rend and Onyxia timers are right again.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Gold totals across your characters are right again."},{"t":"FPS on the stats bar updates again."},{"t":"Routes pasted from Discord or a text file now import.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Fixed an error when a trinket swap failed with an empty trinket slot."},{"t":"Fixed an 'action blocked' error in combat."}]}],"titles":{"forever":"Raid buff tracker, hotswap queue, smoother swaps"}},{"v":"4.7.9","d":"2026-09-28","title":"Route fixes, bar visibility and a simpler colour editor","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Routes no longer skip ahead when you kill mobs that belong to a later step.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Editing a route mid-raid keeps you on the step you were on.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Routes pick up properly on a fresh run of the same raid.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Bars set to show only in raids or only in cities no longer pop back up when you zone or rest."},{"t":"The Weapons Bar's 'In Cities' option now works."},{"t":"Fire-toasted Bun and Dark Desire are now treated as the same buff, so the bar warns when one would replace the other."},{"t":"The raid profile picker no longer flashes when you pick a profile."},{"t":"Fixed an error from the equipment reminder on some saved settings."}]},{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Battle Shout reminder can now track just your own shout, and show everywhere."},{"t":"Every bar can now be shown only while you are in a group, and you can pick exactly which raids count as 'raids'."},{"t":"Trinket, Weapons and Potions bar settings pages got the same fresh look as the rest."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Battle Shout reminder and tracker 'Inside Raids' now only show inside a raid."},{"t":"Picking a raid profile is now one click."},{"t":"Readycheck has an Edit Mode button to move its frames."},{"t":"The colour editor is much easier to use: search for a colour, click it and adjust it right there with sliders, a hex box or the colour wheel. Changed colours are marked and can be reset one at a time."},{"t":"Mesh sync rules now list every feature with a few simple choices each (settings, position, look, saved data), with tabs and a search box."},{"t":"Settings pages were tidied up: clearer labels, confirmations before anything is deleted, and less clutter."}]}],"titles":{"forever":"Bar visibility and a simpler colour editor"}},{"v":"4.7.8","d":"2026-09-21","title":"New look","s":[{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Every window, menu and pop-up has been given a cleaner, flatter look that matches across the whole addon."},{"t":"Boss pages now put all the abilities and gear options in one row along the top. Click one and its settings open underneath, full width.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Trash pages work the same way now.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Ability settings can be copied to every other boss in the raid with one button.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Green now means something is switched on, gold means it is the one you are looking at. They no longer get mixed up together."},{"t":"Menus with nothing in them now say so, and tell you where to add something."}]}]},{"v":"4.7.7","d":"2026-09-05","title":"Minor bug fixes","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"A few small fixes."}]}]},{"v":"4.7.6","d":"2026-08-27","title":"Minor bug fixes","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"A handful of small fixes."}]}]},{"v":"4.7.5","d":"2026-08-22","title":"Split into smaller addons, buff warnings that travel further, and a fuller equipment reminder","s":[{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Readycheck is now split into more addons, so you can switch off the bits you do not use from the AddOns list. Your settings stay put either way."},{"t":"The equipment reminder now shows everything it has flagged at once. Before, if more than one watched item was on - a shield and a utility item, say - you only ever saw one of them. Up to nine can show now."},{"t":"The extra icons pack into the same box you sized in the options, so the reminder takes up no more of your screen with six items than it did with one. The label underneath only fits when a single icon is showing, so it steps aside when there is more than one."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Warnings that a world buff is about to drop now reach your other characters. Before, the warning only travelled to people in your guild or group, so a character in a different guild never got the countdown. Rend, Onyxia, Nefarian and Zandalar warnings now go out to your linked accounts as well.","g":["era"]},{"t":"A buff warning now tells you whether it came from your guild or from your linked accounts.","g":["era"]},{"t":"The equipment reminder no longer goes stale. Equipping a watched item that is not a weapon - a belt, chest or trinket - now updates the reminder straight away, instead of leaving the old icon up until you next changed weapons."},{"t":"Turning off the buff timer network now works. The tickboxes on that page were saving the wrong thing, so unticking one turned it on. Anything left in a mess gets reset to off when you log in.","g":["era"]},{"t":"That switch also works straight away now instead of needing a reload, and the page updates as you click.","g":["era"]},{"t":"You can use /wbtnet on, off or toggle from chat. /wbtnet diag tells you why nothing is syncing.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Gold from your other characters no longer disappears from the gold list after a few minutes."},{"t":"Characters you hear about second-hand no longer lose their race."},{"t":"The new addons switch themselves on when you update, even if your addon manager installed them turned off. Anything you had already turned off by hand stays off."}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"Split into smaller addons, and a fuller equipment reminder","forever":"Split into smaller addons, and a fuller equipment reminder"}},{"v":"4.7.4","d":"2026-08-16","title":"World Tools, Buff Timer Network and a smarter trinket swap","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"New World Tools section. Buff Drops shows timer bars and plays a sound when a world buff is about to drop. Automation can accept summons, click through gossip, and do common turn-ins for you.","g":["era"]},{"t":"New Buff Timer Network page. See when Rend, Onyxia, Nefarian and Songflower are coming up on each layer, shared between Readycheck users. No separate addon needed.","g":["era"]},{"t":"New Target Range tab on the Nameplates page. Add a mob and your nameplate distance changes to what you picked while you target it, then goes back to normal."},{"t":"Smart Macros can now write the macro for you. Pick an action, type a name, and it shows you the finished macro. No macro knowledge needed."},{"t":"Smart macro rules can check more things: a specific boss or mob, world boss, elite, enemy, friendly, not-undead, or no target. One rule can hold up to five of these. A rule can also need an item in your bags that is ready to use."},{"t":"Farm route steps can now do things when you finish them: swap a gear set or trinket, equip an item, or remind you to pot - with a sound, an icon, and an optional delay. Steps can be copied, and the mob picker can filter by wing."},{"t":"The sync page now lets you pick single settings, not just whole groups. New Only button sends just one thing. New preset buttons send or receive everything or nothing. The page tells you in plain words what this character sends."},{"t":"Nameplate settings, the world buff board, your docked gear buttons, the sync transfer bar's position, and the Buff Timer Network settings can now sync between accounts."},{"t":"Smart macros can now be set to only run in Onyxia's Lair, Zul'Gurub or Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj, and every raid's trash is now sorted into wings.","g":["era"]},{"t":"/rc mesh now lists what you send and receive by name. /rc mesh undo puts your old send choices back."},{"t":"If part of the addon is turned off in the AddOns list, you now get a login message saying what is missing and how to turn it back on."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Trinket auto-swap is smarter. It waits for your cast to finish, finishes blocked swaps after combat, grabs whichever trinket is ready sooner, saves the slot for a Priority trinket, and stops pointless back-and-forth swapping on shared cooldowns."},{"t":"Queue order now matters for trinket auto-swap: when more than one trinket is ready, the one higher in the queue wins."},{"t":"If you equip a trinket yourself, the auto-swap now leaves it alone until that trinket has done its job."},{"t":"A smart macro's raid setting now sits on the macro, not on each rule. If you had set it per rule, set it once on the macro instead."},{"t":"The minimap button is now named Readycheck in addons that collect minimap buttons. You may need to grab or hide it again in those addons."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"The docked button spacing slider now keeps its value after a reload."},{"t":"Macros using the addon's old name fix themselves next time you log in."},{"t":"Gear sets that unequip a slot now finish after combat instead of quietly giving up, and tell you when your bags are full."},{"t":"Boss trinket swaps can no longer be yanked out mid-swap by the auto-swapper, and a passive trinket can no longer get a slot stuck forever."},{"t":"Swapping in a trinket that was in your other slot no longer locks the pushed-out trinket in place."},{"t":"Spamming a gear set macro no longer fires the swap over and over."},{"t":"Sync errors now say what went wrong in plain words - wrong password, config too big and which one, or where to go to retry."},{"t":"Moving things is now pixel perfect. Dragging snaps to real screen pixels, and each arrow press in the mover moves exactly one pixel, at any UI scale."},{"t":"The Berserking troll racial now tracks for warriors and rogues. Each class has its own version of the spell, and only the caster classes' version was being watched."},{"t":"Gear buttons you line up by hand no longer drift out of alignment after a reload."},{"t":"While remote editing someone's raid config, creating, deleting, renaming, merging, importing or exporting a profile now works on their config instead of failing with 'profile does not exist'.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"In /rc moveui, the box around a group of docked buttons now sits over the buttons instead of off to one side, and dropping it puts them exactly where you left the box."},{"t":"Snowballs are now tracked in the consumables checker under Utilities & Tools, with a recommended count of 5."},{"t":"Trinket reminders, utility items, post-death consumables, defensive cooldowns and bulk trash edits now change the config of the character you are remote editing. They were quietly editing your own settings instead, then reporting success.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The route page's boss gear set picker now edits the config you have open when remote editing, instead of moving the gear set out of their route and into your own boss setup.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Opening a trash page while remote editing no longer stamps your own race and class onto your profile.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Editing someone's raid config remotely now keeps syncing. Only your first change was being sent - everything after it was silently dropped for several minutes as a duplicate, so sliders, checkboxes and timers looked like they stopped working.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Deleting, renaming or merging a profile while remote editing now actually reaches the other character. Only the profile they had open was ever sent, so removed profiles used to live on forever on their end.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Switching raid profile from the zone-in popup or the boss notes page always switches your own profile, even with a remote edit window open.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Renaming someone else's raid profile no longer renames your own boss notes.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Settings that arrive from another character now take effect straight away. They were being saved but nothing on screen moved until you reloaded, which looked exactly like sync not working."},{"t":"Chat reliably tells you what arrived when a sync lands - one line per sender, listing the categories. Automatic syncs never announced themselves before, only manual pushes did."},{"t":"Changing a setting your character isn't set to send now tells you so once, instead of silently doing nothing."}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"A smarter trinket swap, and macros that write themselves","forever":"A smarter trinket swap, and macros that write themselves"}},{"v":"4.7.3","d":"2026-08-08","title":"Import without the crash","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Importing settings no longer crashes the game. Export strings are much shorter now."},{"t":"Vulture Gizzard is now counted in your bags."},{"t":"The voice warning no longer says oil when a sharpening stone is about to fall off your weapon."}]}]},{"v":"4.7.2","d":"2026-08-06","title":"Minor bug fixes","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Trinkets equipped by a boss gear swap can no longer be swapped off by the trinket auto-swap while the boss is alive - including trinkets that come from the full gear set, not just the per-slot overrides.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The missing-consumables warning on raid entry now only lists items you have none of, instead of also naming things you are merely low on."},{"t":"The raid-entry warning no longer claims weapon stones are missing when the stones are sitting in your bags."},{"t":"Polarity Mode now counts from the moment the boss is actually engaged, so the potion and dummy reminders land at the same instant every single pull. The potion reminder now sits at 5 seconds out of the box.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Using a Blasted Lands buff or a Zanza potion now hides all the others as conflicting on the consumables bar, in both directions.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Right-clicking an item in the consumables checker once again opens the recommended-amount editor, so you no longer have to dig through the settings page."}]}]},{"v":"4.7.1","d":"2026-08-03","title":"Speaks your language","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Readycheck is now translated: German, French, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Russian, Korean and Chinese clients see the menus, pages and buttons in their own language."},{"t":"Russian, Korean and Chinese clients automatically get a font that can display their language."},{"t":"The consumables, potions, weapons and trinket bars can now show item tooltips on hover - off by default, with a checkbox on each bar's settings page."},{"t":"The sync rules page was rebuilt: choose exactly what each connected account sends and receives, category by category."},{"t":"New sync choices for stats bar looks, enchant preferences and farm routes."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The Nameplate Debuffs page is now called Nameplates, and its groups collapse so the page stays short."},{"t":"Choosing who you accept data from now lives in one place on the Network tab."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Syncing between accounts is faster and more reliable, with less chat traffic."}]}]},{"v":"4.7.0","d":"2026-07-31","title":"Raid pages and weapon buttons","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Boss and trash pages redesigned: pick an ability or mob on the left, set it up on the right.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Anything already set up shows a green marker."},{"t":"The consumables bar now has Main Hand, Off Hand and Bag Weapon buttons - the full weapon set without needing the Weapons Bar."},{"t":"Right-click a weapon button to pick which stone or oil to use. The menu opens toward the middle of the screen."},{"t":"Right-click now uses regular consumables just like left-click."},{"t":"Mark must-have items as Priority (right-click an item in the checker) and optionally have the raid-entry warning only mention those."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Route tracker no longer skips ahead when mobs with the same name live in more than one wing.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Right-clicking a weapon button no longer applies the stone."},{"t":"Weapon buttons now work for every class and for staves - healers get their mana oil."},{"t":"A used consumable can no longer stay invisible on the bar."},{"t":"Fixed an error when zoning into a raid with the missing-consumables warning on."},{"t":"Clicking trash mobs no longer closes the wrong section.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The settings window is faster and no longer slows down the game over long sessions."}]}],"titles":{"forever":"Weapon buttons"}},{"v":"4.6.9","d":"2026-07-30","title":"One trinket system","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Ctrl-click a bar trinket to make it first in the queue."},{"t":"Pick your own trinket button clicks - only add the ones you want to change."},{"t":"/rc equip(Item Name,13) - equip or queue any item from a macro."},{"t":"Zone into a raid missing consumables and it shows on screen."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Route can't skip ahead when extra trash dies.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Queued trinkets look the same everywhere."},{"t":"Queue badge shows on the slot being replaced."},{"t":"One queued icon on dock trinkets, not two."},{"t":"Food from your bags starts the bar timer."},{"t":"Eating again refreshes the timer."},{"t":"No more black squares after using stuff in combat."},{"t":"Dockable buttons move with the UI mover."},{"t":"Trinket settings page error fixed."},{"t":"Custom trinket order stays put."},{"t":"Boss death trinkets can't get overwritten by the auto swapper.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Shift-click cancels queued trinkets on dock buttons."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"One trinket queue system everywhere."},{"t":"Click your equipped trinket to use it; click others to equip."},{"t":"Right-click dock buttons to use them; Alt+Left locks."},{"t":"Move mode highlights are subtler."}]}]},{"v":"4.6.8","d":"2026-07-29","title":"Ability reminders for every class","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Ability reminders for every class - each class gets its own list of raid abilities to set up per boss. You only see what your character actually knows.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Racials for everyone - Stoneform, Escape Artist, Will of the Forsaken, War Stomp, and more."},{"t":"Type /rc abilities to see your class list."},{"t":"Drag route steps to reorder them.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Gear Set button border: green = wearing it, gold = own it, red = missing pieces."},{"t":"Dockable buttons can be moved in move mode."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Stats bar shows up at login again and can't get stuck off screen."},{"t":"Boss kill-time display works on its own, and long boss names fit.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Sapphiron bar matches the pull countdown.","g":["era"]},{"t":"World Buffs board: no more vanishing toons, same list on every client, logouts show within seconds. /rc wb purge clears old junk.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Weapon bar clicks work again."},{"t":"Deselecting a boss no longer swaps your gear back.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Troll Berserking shows for all classes."},{"t":"Dropdowns open on top like they should."},{"t":"Fixed some login errors."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Disabled addon parts hide their menu pages."},{"t":"Logging out shows on other toons instantly."}]}]},{"v":"4.6.7","d":"2026-07-25","title":"The voice update, rock-solid sync and speedrun routes","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Natural speech is the voice of everything now - loud, clear, in the voice you pick, working out of the box with no extra downloads. The recorded voice pack is an optional extra for anyone who prefers it."},{"t":"Ready calls are short category words: Trinket ready, Item ready, Potion ready - and Stone, Oil and Potion on the bars. Potion strictly means the real shared-cooldown potions. Every bar item row now has a Say box next to its TTS toggle - type your own spoken name there and it wins over everything."},{"t":"Boss and trash notes can be read aloud, with a Speak button on every note editor to preview from anywhere.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The route catches up when the raid gets ahead of it, and its ready call covers every on-use item it equips - not just trinkets.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Shift+left-click cancels queued swaps: a slot button for that slot only, the Gear Set button for the whole queued set. When a full set is queued, shift-clicking a slot now removes just that slot from the coming swap (click again to restore it) - and clicking a slot with nothing queued is silent instead of chatty."},{"t":"Targeting a boss whose setup uses a full gear set plus slot overrides now equips each slot exactly once: the set skips the overridden slots instead of equipping its own weapon or offhand first and re-swapping it moments later.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"If TrinketMenu runs alongside, the Trinket Manager page says so instead of the two addons silently fighting over your slots."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Speedrun-proof kill detection: chain-pulled packs, simultaneous deaths and look-alike mobs from other wings all count correctly, and the route can no longer skip a run of steps by mistake.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Chronoboon reading is exact - every stored buff shows its own remaining time, Sayge's Dark Fortune included - and world buff timers can no longer drift when the game changes.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Names no longer vanish from the World Buffs window, and other characters' rows stay put while they are offline.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Re-booning updates the window immediately: grabbing fresh buffs into the chronoboon no longer shows the previous boon's contents until you hover it.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Mesh sync is finally quiet: characters verify first and send only what the other is missing. The endless re-syncing on every reload is gone at its root, and several accounts can log in together cleanly."},{"t":"Speech never repeats itself, never reads raid icons aloud, and never goes silent - lines without a recording speak naturally at full volume."},{"t":"Berserking reminders clear on cast for every class."},{"t":"Buttons that could be hovered but not clicked after the game patch work everywhere again."},{"t":"Frames move flush to screen edges, dropdown menus stay attached while scrolling, search leaves no ghost text behind, and Save & Lock recovers a stuck mover."},{"t":"The TTS settings page is reorganized around the new voice system."},{"t":"Under the hood, every tooltip the addon reads (enchant labels, weapon stones, chronoboon contents) now goes through one shared modern reader with a single fallback - one pattern, one place to fix."},{"t":"Under the hood, the addon reads buffs through the game's modern named fields everywhere - the whole class of patch-shifted timers is closed for good - and buff-change handling wakes systems only when a buff they care about actually changed, cutting invisible work during heavy raid combat."}]}],"titles":{"forever":"The voice update and rock-solid sync"}},{"v":"4.6.6","d":"2026-07-22","title":"ItemRack import","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Import your ItemRack gear sets with one click - button on the Gear Manager settings page, shown only while ItemRack is enabled. Sets come over exactly as they were, and your existing sets are never overwritten."},{"t":"Shift+left-click a gear button to cancel that slot's queued after-combat swap, and shift+left-click the Gear Set button to cancel a whole queued set (toggle in Gear Manager settings)."},{"t":"Docked button spacing slider in Gear Manager settings - live preview, 0 restores the classic look."},{"t":"Trinket bar option to pin equipped trinkets to the front - now OFF by default."}]}]},{"v":"4.6.5","d":"2026-07-19","title":"Pinned buttons and Horde Mode","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Pin a gear set or a single item as its own one-click button: Alt+click it in the gear menus. Unlock and hit the X to remove one."},{"t":"The big trinket button now shows the active config's trinkets under its name."},{"t":"Option to swap the trinket button's clicks: left opens the menu, right toggles it. Off by default."},{"t":"Trinket bar option to show only bag trinkets."},{"t":"A progress bar for big syncs - one for sending, one for receiving - with a time estimate."},{"t":"Readycheck also works on Burning Crusade Anniversary realms."},{"t":"Readycheck has its own icon in the AddOns list now."},{"t":"Moving frames works with the game's new Edit Mode: open it and every Readycheck frame gets a drag handle. A small button under the Edit Mode window opens the full mover panel."},{"t":"The profiler now shows CPU numbers measured by the game itself."},{"t":"The Naowh font is included in the font list."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Horde characters start with Horde Mode on, and Horde Mode now hides main hand stone and oil buttons on every bar."},{"t":"Stone buttons only show for classes that use stones."},{"t":"The stone picker is one searchable list instead of a wall of buttons."},{"t":"The trinket bar keeps your equipped trinkets first and no longer shuffles around when you swap."},{"t":"Syncing is faster and much quieter: only new kills are sent, all raids go in one batch, every online character receives at once, and once everyone matches it goes silent."},{"t":"If a sync fails to arrive, both characters say so in chat and it re-sends itself - no more fake Received messages."},{"t":"Sync chat messages are one color."},{"t":"The frame mover lists every movable frame, even ones you have not opened yet."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Wiping your kill history or raid configs on one character now refills properly from your others - no more blank Default raid page after a sync."},{"t":"Two characters on the same account no longer overwrite each other's gear sets just because the sets share a name."},{"t":"Button settings, name text and the lock now apply on your other characters right after syncing instead of fighting the old values."},{"t":"Route changes sync right away instead of waiting for the next login, and a few settings that never synced at all now do - route tracker settings, stats bar picks, enchant picks and the Raid Planner."},{"t":"A character no longer shows up twice on the world buff board.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Broken or missing fonts no longer turn text invisible after the patch - they fall back to the standard font and tell you."},{"t":"Closing the frame mover with Escape no longer leaves the drag handles stuck until a reload."},{"t":"The weapons bar stone list no longer errors and shows every stone and oil."},{"t":"Buttons that use items - gear buttons, trinkets, the consumable bars and the reload button after an import - respond to clicks again after the patch."}]}]},{"v":"4.6.4","d":"2026-07-14","title":"Route tracker, sync stability & smarter equips","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"A boss can switch your trinket auto-swap config when it dies - set it on the boss's Gear tab under After Boss Dies.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The route tracker has prev/next step arrows with a visibility slider and position picker, and can be unlocked and dragged anywhere.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The tracker can preview upcoming steps, with a depth slider.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Duplicate items with different enchants are distinct and pinnable - in the route slot picker (small green line under the name) and on the Speed Item Swaps page. Every equip grabs the pinned copy."},{"t":"New voice calls, each with a switch: Potion ready when the shared cooldown ends, and Use it when a route-equipped trinket comes off cooldown."},{"t":"Raid config weapon swaps can move a weapon worn in your other hand.","g":["era","tbc"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Clicking a spell no longer throws Interface action failed. The addon was writing over Blizzard globals; it no longer writes any."},{"t":"Running several characters at once no longer disconnects you - sync stays under the rate limit and heartbeats jump ahead of bulk data."},{"t":"The tracker reads shorter: names compress, a next step on the same boss shows only its verb, the kill count always shows, and gear swaps no longer take over the display.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Reminders skip items already on cooldown, potions respect the shared lockout, and any potion - right or wrong - advances a potion step."},{"t":"Reloading no longer re-equips step gear over what you put on by hand, and speed item swap-back survives reloads."},{"t":"Sim, Test Actions and manual advance apply raid-config gear exactly like real events: set first, then overrides win their slots, fast and verified.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The engi reminder picker is populated again and the Target Dummy variants are one combined entry."}]}],"titles":{"forever":"Sync stability & smarter equips"}},{"v":"4.6.3","d":"2026-07-13","title":"Raid Route","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"New Raid Route feature: build a kill-order plan for a raid - trash packs to count and bosses as checkpoints - and the addon follows along as you clear, swapping gear and trinkets and showing reminders exactly when each step completes. Open a raid in the sidebar and click the new Route tab. Off by default; turn it on per character from that page.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"A route builder map for Naxxramas: click bosses and trash packs in your kill order to lay out the whole run, and reorder or trim it right there.","g":["era"]},{"t":"While a route is running, a small movable tracker follows along: the current step at the top, its action icons and reminders inside the frame, and an optional dim line showing the next step at the bottom. The frame hugs its content (long text wraps, nothing is ever clipped), a Basic mode strips it down to icons and only the text that matters, the background can be made fully transparent, and scale is the one size control. When a step equips gear, a brief 'Equipping' flash bridges it to the next step - and if the step completed in combat, that flash waits for the swap at the end of combat.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Each step fires everything it carries - gear swaps, trinkets, reminders, spoken alerts - at the moment its own trigger completes: the kill count filling for trash, or the chosen pull/kill event for bosses. Swaps queue safely to the end of combat when you're fighting. Reminders picked from your bags - potions, sappers, dynamite and other consumables - disappear the moment you actually use the item; a step carrying usable items holds until you've used ALL of them (or the next step's requirements complete), and spoken alerts read one compact line per step, always at the step's own completion, cutting off cleanly when the route moves on.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Steps can count several different mobs at once, equip a full gear set, individual trinkets, or any mix of equipment slots, and your progress survives reloads and disconnects. Boss pulls automatically put the plan back on track after wipes or skipped packs.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The world buff board tracks the Darkmoon Faire fortune lockout per character: it counts down only while that character is logged in, pauses on logout, clears after 8 straight hours logged out in a major city, and clears early if a full debuff bar pushes it off.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Fire Festival buffs appear on the world buff board only while someone shown actually has them, and a '60s only' switch (on by default) keeps low-level alts off the board.","g":["era"]},{"t":"The consumables bar's blank-when-used-in-combat behaviour is now a toggle (on by default), and the route tracker's gold accent stripe can be turned off."},{"t":"Routes can be shared three ways now: an Export/Import string on the Route page, a Mesh Share button that pushes the route to every online mesh member instantly, and full remote editing - fetch a raider's config and build their route for them, live.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Trash notes rebuilt from scratch: add each note yourself, pick exactly which trash mobs it watches (whole packs or single mobs, in any mix), write the text, then choose its trigger - fire once after a set number of kills and show for a set duration, or show whenever one of its mobs is your target. Targeting one of a note's mobs displays it silently; the note SPEAKS when its kill requirement is met. Existing blanket, pack and per-mob trash notes carry over automatically. Boss notes use the same add-a-boss flow now instead of listing every boss with an empty editor.","g":["era","tbc"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"The weapon oil picker now offers every oil - Brilliant, Blessed, regular, Lesser and Minor Wizard and Mana Oils and more - instead of a fixed handful."},{"t":"Typing in the custom item ID boxes on the potions and consumables pages no longer gets its focus stolen or interrupted by the search filter."},{"t":"Dropdown menus no longer stay stuck open when the panel refreshes behind them."},{"t":"A gear set saved with empty slots now strips everything in a single click instead of one item per press."},{"t":"Hotswap is out-of-combat only, as it always effectively was: pressing it in combat now just prints your combat message instead of pretending to queue."},{"t":"Characters on the same game account finally share world buff, songflower and fortune data reliably: logging out no longer wiped the session's recorded buffs, so your alts show what they really have.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Sapphiron opener timers no longer start when you Bloodrage before the pull - entering combat by yourself doesn't count anymore; the countdown anchors to Sapphiron actually engaging.","g":["era"]},{"t":"FIXED THE RAID-CONFIG EATER: opening remote edit ran an old cleanup that deleted a raid's entire local config whenever it referenced a gear set name this character doesn't have - and gear sets are per-character, so configs synced from your other toons tripped it constantly. The deletion then synced account-wide. The cleanup is gone, raid deletions no longer propagate over mesh at all, and profile loads keep an automatic safety backup.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Raid configs can no longer LOOK deleted: when the active profile pointer names a profile that no longer exists (rename or sync drift), the addon switches to your richest existing profile and says so, instead of silently creating a blank one over intact data.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"World Buffs presence is now unified with Mesh Sync: any message a character sends over the mesh counts as its board freshness, so unchanged characters send ZERO world-buff traffic between real changes.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Darkmoon Faire buff cooldown: when NovaWorldBuffs is installed, its per-character DMF tracking is used directly.","g":["era"]},{"t":"World Buffs mesh traffic cut hard with many characters online: unchanged 30-second heartbeats shrink to a tiny presence ping (full state goes out on change or every 5 minutes), only ONE toon gossips the offline roster per login event instead of all of them at once, and the background roster re-broadcast drops from every 90 seconds to a 10-minute safety net. Same board, same offline visibility, a fraction of the data.","g":["era"]},{"t":"World Buffs updates arrive faster with many characters online: your own fresh buff changes now jump the shared mesh send queue instead of waiting behind roster relays and config syncs, and the login-time relay burst is spread out so it can't clog things.","g":["era"]},{"t":"World Buffs board: duplicate character rows are merged automatically on every login (case drift and bare-name/realm-name twins fold together, richest record wins) - no more cache wipes, so the board also stops starting empty and slowly refilling after updates.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Text reminders show a note icon instead of the red question mark, and a held step whose gear swap has landed moves on automatically - out of combat about a second after the swap, in combat right after the regen-edge worker equips it. Steps with a use-item still wait for the use."},{"t":"Quick character swaps sync reliably now: logging out of one character and straight into another used to beat the login-sync timers, so data only flowed one way. The push fires fast enough to win that race in both directions."},{"t":"Notes filed under renamed profiles are recovered AUTOMATICALLY on login - no command needed. They're copied into your current profiles wherever those have no note of their own.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Renaming a raid profile now carries every boss and trash note with it - renames used to orphan notes under the old profile name, which read as deletion.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Fixed the real cause of vanishing notes: syncing between your characters was REPLACING the whole notes store, wiping any per-profile notes the sending character didn't have. Sync now merges notes additively - nothing local is ever deleted - so logging each character once restores the account to the union of everyone's notes. A one-time cleanup also removes the wrong Default-profile copies an earlier repair spread around, and rescues AQ20 notes stranded by the old migration.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Route tracker text is never cut off: lines WRAP within the tracker's width instead of truncating with '...'. Width comes from its slider (plus scale); height follows the wrapped content and the frame grows DOWNWARD only - the top edge stays pinned where you placed it. The height slider is gone because height takes care of itself.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"A route ENDING on a boss step now finishes properly: the checkpoint path used to skip the whole finish - no 'Route complete' line, no spoken alert, tracker just vanished. Both completion paths finish identically now.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Boss checkpoint steps now get the same 2-second 'Done' hold that kill steps get - completing a boss step (pulled or killed, simmed or real) shows what just finished on the tracker's main line with the next gate underneath, instead of flipping instantly.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"New /rc notesdump command prints every stored boss and trash note key so note issues are diagnosable on the spot.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Route reminders live entirely inside the tracker now - one frame, one entry in /rc moveui. The separate reminder plaque under it is gone; test fires render in the same frame too.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The Remote Raid Config page matches normal raid editing: pick the toon, then click a raid - each raid is a one-click row showing its fetch or local-copy status inline.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Naxxramas gargoyles are named correctly: Plagued Gargoyle in the Spider and Military wings, Stoneskin Gargoyle in the Plague wing. If a saved route step or trash note referenced the wrong one for its wing, re-pick the mob in the editor.","g":["era"]},{"t":"Switching between characters on one account now triggers a full sync in both directions every time, and the world buff roster arrives together with it."}]}],"titles":{"forever":"Fixes"}},{"v":"4.6.2","d":"2026-07-02","title":"Kill history & Darkmoon Faire accuracy","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"You can now add many kill times at once. Next to the add-kill box there's a new Bulk button that opens a window where you can paste a whole list of times - like 1:32 105 2:03 - separated by spaces, commas or new lines. It shows how many kills it found and their average before you commit, and one click records them all.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"When adding kills by hand - one at a time or in bulk - you can now mark them as having the Darkmoon Faire damage buff so they count toward the right averages. The add-kill row has a small orb you can light up, and the bulk window has a matching checkbox.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Editing a recorded kill now lets you correct whether the Darkmoon Faire buff was active for that kill.","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"The kill data browser now labels its Darkmoon Faire column, so the small orb next to a kill clearly means the buff was up for it.","g":["era","tbc"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Kill time predictions now respect the Darkmoon Faire buff everywhere. The on-screen kill timer, pace comparisons, reminders that fire based on remaining fight time, and boss simulations all prefer averages from kills with the same buff state you have now, falling back to all kills when there isn't enough matching data.","g":["era","tbc"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Old kill records that could no longer be matched to a raid and boss are now removed automatically instead of piling up. The 'Unrecognized Data' section is gone.","g":["era","tbc"]}]}]},{"v":"4.6.1","d":"2026-06-27","title":"Repair reminder, gear tooltips & fixes","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"The gear set button now warns you when a set is missing gear. If you don't have everything a set needs (worn or sitting in your bags), its name turns red, and its tooltip marks each missing piece and shows a 'missing gear' note - so you can tell at a glance which sets you can fully equip."},{"t":"Changing the size of the dockable gear buttons now shows a reminder that a UI reload is needed for the new size to take effect, with a Reload UI button right there so you can do it on the spot. It never reloads on its own."},{"t":"When your gear durability gets low, a repair reminder now appears on screen - an anvil icon with a 'Repair' label, shown where your other reminders appear - instead of only a chat message. It flags a repair when your overall durability or any single piece of gear drops below the threshold you set, it checks when you log in and when you enter a raid, and it clears once you repair."},{"t":"You can now turn tooltips on or off for the dockable gear buttons and their hover menus, with an option to show them only while you are out of combat. They are off by default."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"While you're in combat, a consumable's icon now disappears the moment you use it, so a consumable you've already used reads as spent and you won't waste a click trying to use it again. This covers everything on the bar - potions stay hidden while they're on cooldown, and flasks, elixirs and food (which have no cooldown) stay hidden until their buff drops or combat ends. Out of combat the bar always looks normal."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Fixed the Trinket bar moving to the wrong spot after a reload when you positioned it with the UI Mover. Dragging the bar directly already worked; the UI Mover now saves its position correctly too."},{"t":"Fixed Mesh Network sync so that logging a character in while another of your characters is already online now reliably sends the online character's synced data to the one that just logged in. This previously failed when the online character still had the other flagged as connected, and it now also works when several of your characters are online at the same time."},{"t":"Equipping a gear set that uses two of the same weapon - or two identical rings or trinkets - now puts one copy in each slot instead of trying to fit a single item into both."},{"t":"Fixed a grey edge that could appear along the top and left of the dockable gear buttons at certain UI scales."},{"t":"The hover menus on the dockable gear buttons now match the size of the buttons themselves."},{"t":"When gear button tooltips are turned on, they now appear cleanly beside the hover menu instead of partly hidden behind it."}]}]},{"v":"4.6.0","d":"2026-06-19","title":"Weapon toggles & search fixes","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"The Weapons bar now lets you turn each weapon on or off individually. Open the Weapons tab and click a weapon's icon to show or hide it. This works for both your equipped weapons and your sharpenable bag weapons, and the icons update on their own when your weapons change."},{"t":"The Consumables bar now has the same per-weapon icons, so you can choose exactly which weapons it tracks."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Bag weapons now show on the Weapons bar by default."},{"t":"The search boxes inside settings panels now match the look of the main sidebar search."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"The Consumables bar now applies your weapon stone or oil even when the Weapons bar's click action is set to Nothing."},{"t":"The Consumables bar and Weapons bar now control their bag weapons separately. Turning bag weapons off on one bar no longer turns them off on the other."},{"t":"Fixed a settings search box that could cause lag or leave the keyboard stuck until you reloaded."},{"t":"Fixed a settings search box stealing the cursor from the main sidebar search while you were typing in it."}]}]},{"v":"4.5.9","d":"2026-06-15","title":"Weapon bar equipping & sidebar search upgrades","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"The Consumables, Potions and Weapons bar lists, and the warrior talent list, now have a search box at the top so you can filter long lists by typing part of a name"},{"t":"Sidebar search now finds individual settings and options, not just pages - searching things like 'text to speech', 'reminder sound' or 'weapon detection' takes you straight to the right place"},{"t":"Equipment Reminder can now give a separate spoken alert for each gear type, such as a missing weapon enchant or the wrong weapon equipped, each with its own repeat setting"},{"t":"Weapon bar buttons can now equip weapons, not just apply stones to them. By default, shift-clicking your equipped main-hand or off-hand button moves that weapon to the other slot, and shift-clicking one of your bagged weapons equips it - and weapon swaps work even during combat"},{"t":"What each click on a weapon bar button does is now fully configurable - left, right, shift-click and ctrl-click can each be set to apply a stone, open the stone picker, equip to main hand, equip to off hand, or do nothing, from the Weapons bar settings"},{"t":"Added a macro builder under Hotswap that creates an equip-this-item-to-this-slot macro - type an item name, pick a slot, and it makes a macro you can drag onto an action bar or bind to a key"}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The Settings menu now expands to list its pages when selected, the same as the other menu sections, and the window opens straight to General & Behavior instead of a welcome screen"},{"t":"What's New now has its own page in the sidebar"},{"t":"Sidebar search no longer floods with results - it shows the most relevant matches first and a hint to type more when there are too many to list"},{"t":"Removed a large amount of unused code under the hood to keep the addon leaner"},{"t":"Reminders now use a single clean fade in and out. The other animation styles (pulse, flash, glow, bounce, shake, grow and slide) have been retired - they kept animating the whole time a reminder was on screen, which could cost frames during busy fights. If you had one of those styles selected, it has been switched to fade automatically."},{"t":"The animation style dropdown and the per-ability animation overrides have been removed. The Fade In Duration and Fade Out Duration sliders now live under the Behavior tab in Reminder Settings."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Holding Backspace in a search box now keeps deleting instead of stopping after one character"},{"t":"The Mesh Network password box now stays hidden behind dots when you click into it, and you can still highlight it and copy it with Ctrl+C without revealing it"},{"t":"Importing or exporting your settings now also includes your hotswap gear set and sidebar layout, which were previously left out"},{"t":"Spoken reminders set to repeat now play the correct number of times"},{"t":"Smoother framerate during big fights: sitting down to eat no longer makes every reminder bar do extra work each frame, the Battle Shout party check no longer re-reads tooltips every second, and the trinket swap queue only redraws when something actually changes."},{"t":"The icons on the weapon bar no longer go blank after you swap a weapon during combat"}]}]},{"v":"4.5.8","d":"2026-06-14","title":"OmniCC support & in-combat trinket queue","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"OmniCC support - if you also run OmniCC (or a similar cooldown-number addon), Readycheck now detects it automatically and steps aside on its consumable, potion, weapon and trinket bars and on the dockable gear buttons, letting OmniCC show the countdown numbers there so they no longer double up. With no such addon installed, Readycheck shows its own numbers everywhere as before"},{"t":"Trinket Menu swaps can now be queued in combat - click a trinket while fighting and a small icon appears on the slot it will fill, then it equips automatically the moment you leave combat, the same way queued gear sets work"},{"t":"The Trinket Menu now has a toggle to hide the 1 and 2 slot numbers shown on your equipped trinkets, under its General Settings"}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Sidebar search now finds the Mesh Network, World Buffs and Remote Raid Config pages by more terms, including things like 'stuck', 'cross-faction', 'buff board' and 'remote edit'"},{"t":"The Readycheck chat tag is now shown in gold without the surrounding brackets"}]}]},{"v":"4.5.7","d":"2026-06-12","title":"Cross-faction world buffs","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Cross-faction world buffs - your Alliance and Horde characters can now share world buff status with each other over Battle.net. Turn it on under Connections, add your other account or a Battle.net friend as a cross-faction peer, and their buffs (and yours) show up together in the World Buff Tracker, even across factions and while offline","g":["era"]}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Minor bug fixes and performance improvements"}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"Minor bug fixes","forever":"Minor bug fixes"}},{"v":"4.5.6","d":"2026-06-05","title":"World Buff Tracker & gear override picker","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"World Buff Tracker - open /wb to see which world buffs you and your other characters currently have, including buffs frozen in a Chronoboon. It shows the time left on each, tracks where Songflowers were last picked, and reports your Chronoboon and Hearthstone cooldowns. Buff data is shared over the Mesh Network, so even characters that are offline still show their last-known buffs","g":["era"]},{"t":"The per-slot gear override picker now lists each copy of an item you are carrying, so duplicates like multiple Goblin Rocket Boots all show up instead of collapsing into a single icon"}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Minor bug fixes and performance improvements"}]}],"titles":{"tbc":"Gear override picker","forever":"Gear override picker"}},{"v":"4.5.5","d":"2026-06-01","title":"Consumable reminder fixes & Smart Macro scoping","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Nameplate Debuffs - see key debuffs and procs right on enemy nameplates: armor reduction (Sunder Armor, Expose Armor, Faerie Fire), Overpower availability, Execute range, and more. Fully customizable groups, icon sizes, positions, colors and timers. Turn it on and tune it under Nameplate Debuffs in the sidebar","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Smart Macros can now be limited to a specific raid - and to a specific raid profile within it - with the 'Active in' option. Give several Smart Macros the same in-game macro name, each scoped to a different raid or profile, and that one macro will do different things depending on where you are"},{"t":"A Smart Macro with an empty body now clears (blanks) the in-game macro when its rule fires - handy for switching a macro off while targeting something"},{"t":"Dropdown lists can now be filtered by typing - start typing while a dropdown is open to narrow it instead of scrolling, for example when picking a boss or a trigger type"}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"On-target and post-boss-death consumable reminders now appear correctly","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Consumable reminders no longer show up when the consumable is not in your bags"},{"t":"Consumable reminders no longer disappear before you have a chance to use the consumable"}]}]},{"v":"4.5.4","d":"2026-05-24","title":"Smart Macros & racial reminders","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Smart Macros - create a macro that rewrites itself based on what you are targeting. Set rules for creature type or mob name and the macro updates automatically. Found in the sidebar"},{"t":"Blood Fury (Orc) and Berserking (Troll) are now available as reminder abilities on every boss and trash tab, with full support for all trigger types (target HP%, TTK, combat start, buff remaining, etc.) - only visible to the matching race","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Post-Boss Consumables - configure any consumable (Zanza potions, elixirs, food, buffs, etc.) to remind you to use it either after a boss dies or when you first target the boss. Found in the Utility section of each boss tab. Pick items from a category browser so the list stays manageable","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Food buffs and bandages are now tracked on the consumable bar - toggle them individually in the Items tab. They are also available on the potion bar but hidden by default"},{"t":"Remote raid config editing - open any Mesh Network member in the Raids sidebar and click Edit Config to fetch their full raid setup, edit it directly (boss abilities, gear swaps, timers, notes, everything), then push your changes back to them. Works even if they are offline","g":["era","tbc"]}]}]},{"v":"4.5.3","d":"2026-05-21","title":"Consumable TTS repeat & gear swap fix","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Consumable bar items now have individual TTS and Repeat toggles in the Items tab - enable or disable each consumable independently"},{"t":"Consumable TTS can repeat after the buff expires - set how many times and how long after expiry in the Behavior tab"}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Mesh Network now shows separate sync options for Battle Shout reminder settings and the Battle Shout party tracker, so you can enable each independently"},{"t":"Post-boss gear set no longer fails to swap when adds are still alive when the boss dies(hopefully)","g":["era","tbc"]}]}]},{"v":"4.5.2","d":"2026-05-14","title":"Remote gear editing & fixes","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Remote gear editing - open Gear Manager > Remote tab to view and edit another warrior's gear sets directly, then push your changes to them when they log in"},{"t":"Deleting a gear set now asks whether to remove it locally or also queue the deletion for your other mesh warriors"}]}]},{"v":"4.5.1","d":"2026-05-13","title":"Mesh Network","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Mesh Network - sync your Readycheck settings across multiple accounts or characters automatically. Set up a shared channel name and password and your raid configs, boss notes, gear sets, ML Predictions data, consumables, and more stay in sync in real time"},{"t":"Boss Exclusions in ML Predictions - uncheck any boss to stop recording fight data for it. Per-raid tabs for MC, BWL, AQ40, and Naxx so you are not scrolling through a wall of checkboxes","g":["era","tbc"]}]}]},{"v":"4.5.0","d":"2026-05-06","title":"Bug fixes & improvements","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Fixed some buttons and colors not working right in the settings"},{"t":"Fixed Fungal Bloom gear swaps not working correctly","g":["era"]},{"t":"Trinket auto-swapper no longer swaps off a ready trinket immediately after login or reload"}]},{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Raid profile selector now visible at the top of every boss tab (Abilities, Gear, History)","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"ML Predictions data tab now shows kills from all profiles combined","g":["era","tbc"]},{"t":"Kills in ML Predictions can now be clicked to edit the time and profile","g":["era","tbc"]}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Kill history scrollbar only appears when there are more kills than fit on screen","g":["era","tbc"]}]}]}]},"defaultframes":{"current":"1.1.1","games":["era","tbc","forever","retail"],"versions":[{"v":"1.1.1","d":"2026-11-25","title":"","s":[{"type":"notes","items":[{"t":"The addon has a website for bug reports and feature suggestions: /orf report and /orf suggest give you a link with your version and game filled in, and /orf site opens the list of what changed."},{"t":"Report and Suggest buttons in the options window do the same."}]}]},{"v":"1.1.0","d":"2026-11-22","title":"","s":[{"type":"notes","items":[{"t":"WoW Forever and Retail: the addon now loads and works there as well as on Classic Era and Burning Crusade Anniversary - one folder, the same files. Those clients hide some values from addons during a fight; the README's \"WoW Forever and Retail\" section lists what goes quiet until the value can be read again."},{"t":"Party frames: the same frames for a 5-player group, under a gold \"Party\" title where Group 1 stands in a raid. Display Party Frames and Show Yourself in Party in /orf (or /orf party, /orf partyplayer)."},{"t":"Fixed on WoW Forever: an error from the heal prediction library when it loaded before the game's own aura reader existed."}]}]}]},"stacked":{"current":"1.1.5","games":["era","tbc","forever"],"versions":[{"v":"1.1.5","d":"2026-11-25","title":"","s":[{"type":"notes","items":[{"t":"The addon has a website for bug reports and feature suggestions: /srg report and /srg suggest give you a link with your version and game filled in, and /srg site opens the list of what changed."},{"t":"\"Report a problem\" and \"Suggest a feature\" in the options window do the same."}]}]},{"v":"1.1.4","d":"2026-11-22","title":"","s":[{"type":"notes","items":[{"t":"WoW Forever (1.60.1) support. Forever runs the same Edit Mode raid frames (checked against Blizzard's published 1.60.1 UI source: the group frames, the flow layout and the Edit Mode raid settings are the same code), with three differences this version accounts for:","sub":["its raid container also re-arranges on the game's LFG update event. The combat guard now holds that one too, so a mid-fight LFG update cannot snap the grid back to one line. It is only touched on a client whose container listens for it - nothing changes on Classic Era or Burning Crusade Anniversary.","its raid container re-measures itself one frame after every layout. With \"resize container\" on, the grid's size is put back in that same frame.","the game can hide a frame's size, position or protection from addons there. A layout pass that meets a hidden value is skipped and retried instead of raising an error."]},{"t":"The post-combat \"anything still missing\" note asks the game itself whether Main Tank / Main Assist frames are shown at all (Forever hides them in matchmade raids without role requirements)."},{"t":"Safety net on every client: a layout pass that fails for any reason is reported once in chat and no longer repeats several times a second; /srg status shows the error text and the game build."},{"t":"The shared TOC lists WoW Forever's interface number (16001)."},{"t":"No change to how the layout looks or behaves on Classic Era or Burning Crusade Anniversary."}]}]},{"v":"1.1.3","d":"2026-08-08","title":"","s":[{"type":"notes","items":[{"t":"Burning Crusade Anniversary (2.5.6) support made first-class. The addon now ships client-specific TOC files - StackedRaidGroups_Vanilla.toc (Interface 11509) and StackedRaidGroups_TBC.toc (Interface 20506) - alongside the shared fallback TOC, so both clients mark the addon compatible and addon managers (CurseForge, WowUp) detect both game versions from one package."},{"t":"No gameplay code changes: 2.5.6 runs the same modern raid-frame UI code as 1.15.9 (verified against Blizzard's published 2.5.6 UI source - the compact raid frame container/layout code is identical), so the Lua works unchanged on both clients."},{"t":"README: per-client install instructions; the one-time update note in chat now mentions dual-client support."}]}]},{"v":"1.1.2","d":"2026-08-06","title":"","s":[{"type":"notes","items":[{"t":"Roster changes made DURING combat are now fully reflected the moment combat drops, instead of waiting for the game's next roster event: the addon reconciles group visibility itself at combat end (shows an existing group frame that players moved into mid-fight - its members were kept current the whole time by the group's own handler - and hides a group that emptied mid-fight). Group frames are unprotected, so this is legal and taint-free out of combat."},{"t":"The layout pass now also picks up any shown group frame missing from the game's (stale) internal flow list, so such a group can never be left overlapping the grid."},{"t":"Still deferred to the game's next pass (cannot be created by an addon): brand-new pet frames, Main Tank/Assist changes, and a group frame that has never existed this session."},{"t":"Harness: added no-post-combat-event scenarios (hidden group refilled mid-fight; group emptied mid-fight) - 26 checks pass under both engine behaviors."}]}]},{"v":"1.1.1","d":"2026-08-06","title":"","s":[{"type":"notes","items":[{"t":"Fixed: the layout could stay broken after combat ended and never recover until /reload. Cause: when the engine rejects an in-combat frame move it can raise a hard Lua error (secure anchoring restriction) instead of silently ignoring the call; the error aborted a layout pass halfway and left an internal \"layout in progress\" flag stuck, which silently disabled every future layout pass - including the combat-end repair. All frame-move attempts are now error-isolated (a rejected section is treated as combat-deferred), the watchdog self-heals the stuck flag, and the combat-end repair is ordered so nothing can prevent it from running. This bug predates the combat guard and could also freeze v1.0.0."},{"t":"Verified with an offline test harness that simulates the game's event dispatch, combat lockdown, and both engine behaviors (silent block and hard error) across login, mid-combat logoffs, group emptying, join-into-hidden-group pass-through, and combat-end restore."}]}]},{"v":"1.1.0","d":"2026-08-06","title":"","s":[{"type":"notes","items":[{"t":"Combat guard (new, on by default): mid-combat roster changes - e.g. a player logging off during a pull - no longer snap the raid frames back to the game's single-line layout. While you are in combat the addon unregisters the container's two re-flow trigger events (GROUP_ROSTER_UPDATE / UNIT_PET) on the container frame only; the group frames keep updating their own members through their own secure handlers, so offline greying, leavers hiding, and joiners appearing in visible groups all still work. Everything re-syncs at combat end. Tradeoff: frames that would need to be CREATED mid-fight (brand-new pets, MT/MA changes) appear after combat instead; if a player joins a group with no frame on screen, one roster event is deliberately let through so the game can build it, then the guard re-arms. Toggle: /srg guard on|off, or the options window (/srg)."},{"t":"The engine block probe (whether in-combat group moves are allowed) is now reset every fight instead of once per session."},{"t":"Options window: new \"Combat guard\" toggle under General, with a tooltip explaining exactly what the guard does and its tradeoffs."},{"t":"/srg guard (no argument) prints the same explanation in chat, and a one-time chat note announces the new behavior after updating."},{"t":"README: combat stability section rewritten; stale command lists removed."},{"t":"Stacks the default raid frames' separate groups into rows (e.g. Groups 5-8 directly under Groups 1-4) instead of one long line, for the new Edit Mode raid frames introduced in patch 1.15.9 / 2.5.6. The frames themselves are untouched - position only."},{"t":"Groups per row (1-8), fill order (Groups 1-4 on top, or classic 1,3,5,7 on top with /srg fill columns), spacing, and empty-group handling."},{"t":"Main Tank / Assist and pet sections placeable on any side of the grid, with an option to hide the MT target mini-frames."},{"t":"Options window (/srg), chat commands for everything (/srg help), diagnostics for bug reports (/srg status), a combat-lock heads-up, and a login message (both toggleable)."},{"t":"Known limitation (engine rule for all addons): if the game re-lays out its frames during combat (roster changes, pet frames, MT target churn), the single-line layout can show until combat ends, then the grid restores instantly. See the README for the combat stability checklist."}]}]}]},"wowtiler":{"current":"1.5","games":[],"versions":[{"v":"1.5","d":"2026-11-11","title":"One automatic layout, with the controls that matter","s":[{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The Layout tab is much simpler: the tiler always works out the arrangement that leaves the least empty screen at your chosen aspect, and you steer it with three settings.","sub":["Main goes: Automatic, Left (alts on the right), Right (alts on the left), Top or Bottom.","Mains: how many big windows (1-4).","Alt size: Balanced, Small alts with the biggest main, or Large alts (at least half the main)."]},{"t":"Customize layout still lets you drag your own slots; the new Back to automatic button undoes it."}]},{"type":"removed","items":[{"t":"The list of named layouts, the Main size slider and the Fill the screen option. An old left / right / top / bottom layout choice carries over to the matching Main goes setting."}]},{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"The Keep free boxes and the Mains hint no longer get cut off."}]}]},{"v":"1.4","d":"2026-11-07","title":"Ultrawide support","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Auto layout (now the default): instead of assuming a 16:9 monitor, the tiler tries every candidate arrangement for your screen - 16:9, 21:9 ultrawide, 32:9 super-ultrawide, anything - and keeps the one that leaves the least empty space, with every window still 16:9. On a 3440x1440 with 3 alts that is a full-height 2560x1440 main plus three 853x480 alts (1% empty); on a 5120x1440 with 4 alts it is the main plus a 2x2 of 1280x720 (0% empty). The status bar shows which arrangement it picked. Your existing layout choice is kept; pick Auto from the Layout dropdown to switch."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"The L-shape layout centers its block on wider-than-16:9 screens instead of leaving all the slack on one side."}]}]},{"v":"1.3.3","d":"2026-11-06","title":"","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Window opening as a tiny stub after being minimized to the tray - really fixed this time. Windows kept the minimized placement (an off-screen 199x34 rectangle) while the app believed the window was normal, so the previous check never fired. The app now remembers the last good size and position and forces it back whenever the window would come up collapsed, regardless of what the state flag says."},{"t":"Launching the exe while it is already running no longer swaps a pending update in underneath the running copy."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"WowTiler.log now records the version at startup."}]}]},{"v":"1.3.2","d":"2026-11-06","title":"","s":[{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Update prompt is a real popup. When a newer release exists, the tiler brings its window up with a Yes/No dialog on top (tray balloons get silenced by Windows while a game is running). If you are in Raid mode it waits and asks when you leave it. It also re-checks every 6 hours, so a long session still catches new releases."}]}]},{"v":"1.3.1","d":"2026-11-06","title":"","s":[{"type":"fixed","items":[{"t":"Opening the window from the tray (or by launching the exe again) could show only a tiny title-bar stub if the window had been minimized to the tray. Windows kept the minimized placement; the app now un-minimizes it properly and restores the full size."}]}]},{"v":"1.3","d":"2026-11-06","title":"","s":[{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Mains layouts now solve the split for you. With Mains across the top / Mains on the left, every arrangement of mains grid x alts grid at every size is tried and the one that leaves the least empty screen wins - all windows stay 16:9, alts never bigger than mains. 2 mains + 2 alts becomes a gap-free 2x2; 2 + 3 is two 1920x1080 mains over three 1280x720; 3 mains fill a 2x2 grid with the alts packed into the free quarter. Alts sit flush against the mains so any remainder is one strip at the edge. The Main size slider no longer applies to these layouts."}]}]},{"v":"1.2","d":"2026-11-06","title":"","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Multiple mains. Set Mains (1-4) on the Layout tab and pick Mains across the top or Mains on the left: the mains share the big region equally (all 16:9) and the alts pack smaller beside them. In a Custom layout the first N slots you draw are the mains. Promoting an alt replaces the main you promoted longest ago, so it rotates."}]},{"type":"changed","items":[{"t":"Opening the window from the tray is more robust, and the app now writes WowTiler.log next to the exe. If the window ever fails to open, send that file."},{"t":"Launching the exe while it is already running now tells you if the running copy did not respond."}]}]},{"v":"1.1","d":"2026-11-06","title":"The first public release","s":[{"type":"notes","items":[{"t":"It finds every running WoW window and lays them out on your monitor with one big main and smaller alts, all kept at a true 16:9 so nothing is stretched. Shift+click into any alt (or hit a hotkey) and it becomes the main. Clients that log in or out are picked up automatically. A Raid mode key makes your main full-screen and borderless and brings the layout back when you are done."},{"t":"L-shape or classic layouts, a custom layout editor with a live preview (draw your own slots), alts on a second monitor, reserved screen edges for a stream overlay, per-client opt-out, editable hotkeys, start with Windows (lives in the tray), built-in updater."}]}]}]},"multilauncher":{"current":"1.0.0","games":[],"versions":[{"v":"1.0.0","d":"2026-11-27","title":"First release","s":[{"type":"added","items":[{"t":"Opens every Battle.net account at once, each in its own launcher window, already signed in."},{"t":"Two ways to sign in, picked per account: a saved session with no password, or the email and password typed for you."},{"t":"Emails and passwords are stored encrypted, and the log never names an account."},{"t":"A ready check window ticks each account off as its launcher comes up."},{"t":"Dark and light looks."},{"t":"Can run at Windows login."},{"t":"Used to be called Battalion: your accounts and settings carry over the first time it runs, and it offers to clean up the old files."}]}]}]}}};
